{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1785700047","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-dLrfj37igZyfYsFbyQUi63","dateCreated":"2025-05-27T16:47:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-06-06T16:48:40+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Asia Pacific (Taipei) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/06/amazon-efs-taipei-region/","postDateTime":"2025-06-06T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Amazon EFS is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Taipei) region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1609604097","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-p3WJe8SPjqyLhpavkrA45n","dateCreated":"2025-01-08T18:46:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-02-10T19:05:21+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) has now increased the access points limit from 1,000 to 10,000 per file system, a 10x increase. This launch makes it even easier for customers to manage application-specific access to shared datasets, enabling them to seamlessly scale access management to thousands of users, on a single EFS file system.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAmazon EFS is a fully elastic file storage service that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the AWS cloud. Access points are application-specific entry points that enforce a user identity and root directory, and logically isolate data between applications. The new EFS access point limits automatically apply to all file systems and require no action from customers.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe new access point limits are immediately available in all commercial AWS regions, except in AWS China Regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-access-points.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e or create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, API, or AWS CLI.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/02/amazon-efs-access-points-file-system/","postDateTime":"2025-02-10T10:00:00-08:00","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 10,000 access points per EFS file system"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1651058422","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"oEfQjcjJ9C4cRRd4mawhyV","dateCreated":"2025-01-23T20:06:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-01-23T21:20:53+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Mexico (Central) Region.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/01/amazon-efs-aws-mexico-central-region","postDateTime":"2025-01-23T16:20:00-05:00","headline":"Amazon EFS is now available in the AWS Mexico (Central) Region"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1475484338","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"rhcEabfRsNjf24ebQZzbxs","dateCreated":"2024-11-12T22:19:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-26T22:02:08+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS now supports up to 2.5 million read IOPS and up to 500,000 write IOPS per file system, a 10x increase over the previous limits, making it easier to power machine learning (ML) research, multi-tenant SaaS, genomics, and other data-intensive workloads on AWS.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads on AWS. With this launch, Amazon EFS supports up to 2.5 million read IOPS and up to 500,000 write IOPS per file system. Now, applications that demand millions of IOPS and tens of GiB per second of throughput performance, such as analytics user shares supporting hundreds of data scientists, multi-tenant SaaS applications supporting thousands of customers, and distributed applications processing petabytes of genomics data, can easily scale to achieve the required highest level of performance.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe increased IOPS limits are available for all new EFS General Purpose file systems using the Elastic Throughput mode in all AWS commercial regions, except in AWS China Regions. For new file systems, you can request an IOPS limit increase in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/home/services/elasticfilesystem/quotas\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Service Quota console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e or create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, API, or AWS CLI.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-efs-up-to-2-5-million-iops-per-file-system","postDateTime":"2024-11-26T16:10:00-05:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 2.5 million IOPS per file system"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1476590094","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"2c361WTSntMJi45bvVN4jH","dateCreated":"2024-08-06T21:53:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-08-07T17:03:20+0000","additionalFields":{"headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/08/amazon-efs-30-gibs-read-throughput","postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the AWS cloud. In March 2024, we increased the Elastic Throughput read throughput limit to 20 GiB/s (from 10 GiB/s) to support the growing demand for read-heavy workloads such as AI and machine learning. Now, we are further increasing the read throughput to 30 GiB/s, extending EFS\u0026rsquo;s simple, fully elastic, and provisioning-free experience to support throughput-intensive AI and machine learning workloads for model training, inference, financial analytics, and genomic data analysis.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThe increased throughput limits are immediately available for EFS file systems using the Elastic Throughput mode in the US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU West (Dublin), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Regions. To learn more, see the Amazon EFS Documentation or create a file system using the Amazon EFS Console, API, or AWS CLI.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2024-08-07T13:00:00-04:00","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 30 GiB/s (a 50% increase) of read throughput"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-05-amazon-efs-maximum-per-client-throughput-1-5-gibs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-efs-maximum-per-client-throughput-1-5-gibs/","dateCreated":"2024-05-01T19:19:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:00:39+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS file systems now support up to 1.5 GiB/s of throughput per client, a 3x increase over the previous limit of 500 MiB/s. With this launch, you now have a simpler way to run throughput-intensive file workloads on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that simplifies setting up and running file workloads in the AWS cloud. Starting today, Amazon EFS file systems can now deliver up to 1.5 GiB/s of throughput to a single Amazon EC2 instance or Amazon EKS pod. This performance boost especially benefits throughput-intensive workloads – such as financial analytics, genomics, and video transcoding – that drive high levels of throughput from one or many individual clients. With this launch, you can process data up to 3x faster on Amazon EFS, meaning you can deliver insights more quickly and with lower compute costs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis increased per-client throughput limit is available for all file systems using the EFS Elastic Throughput mode and mounted using the latest version of the Amazon EFS client (amazon-efs-utils) or the Amazon EFS CSI Driver (aws-efs-csi-driver). This performance increase is supported in all commercial AWS Regions at no additional cost. To learn more,\u0026nbsp;see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/getting-started/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-05-01T19:19:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-efs-maximum-per-client-throughput-1-5-gibs/","postDateTime":"2024-05-01T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS increases maximum per-client throughput to 1.5 GiB/s","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS file systems now support up to 1.5 GiB/s of throughput per client, a 3x increase over the previous limit of 500 MiB/s. With this launch, you now have a simpler way to run throughput-intensive file workloads on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-03-amazon-efs-supports-20-gibs-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/03/amazon-efs-supports-20-gibs-throughput/","dateCreated":"2024-03-13T19:01:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:52+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the throughput per file system to up to 20 GiB/s of read throughput and up to 5 GiB/s of write throughput.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the AWS cloud. With Elastic Throughput, Amazon EFS automatically scales throughput performance up or down to meet your application needs, and you only pay for what you use. This launch increases the maximum throughput performance for EFS file systems using Elastic Throughput by up to 2x, to 20 GiB/s of read throughput (from 10 GiB/s) and to 5 GiB/s of write throughput (from 3 GiB/s). With these higher throughput limits, you can now extend EFS’s simple, fully elastic, provisioning-free experience to even more throughput-intensive workloads, such as machine learning, genomics, and data analytics applications.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased throughput limits are immediately available for EFS file systems using the Elastic Throughput mode in the US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), Europe West (Dublin), and Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e or create a file system using the Amazon EFS Console, API, or AWS CLI.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-03-13T19:00:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/03/amazon-efs-supports-20-gibs-throughput/","postDateTime":"2024-03-13T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 20 GiB/s of throughput","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the throughput per file system to up to 20 GiB/s of read throughput and up to 5 GiB/s of write throughput.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-02-amazon-efs-aws-canada-west-calgary-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-efs-aws-canada-west-calgary-region/","dateCreated":"2024-02-16T21:37:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:45:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Canada West (Calgary) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-16T21:36:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/02/amazon-efs-aws-canada-west-calgary-region/","postDateTime":"2024-02-16T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS is now available in the AWS Canada West (Calgary) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Canada West (Calgary) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2024-01-higher-read-iops-amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/higher-read-iops-amazon-elastic-file-system/","dateCreated":"2024-02-02T13:32:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:43:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now delivers 40% higher read IOPS per file system, making it easier to power data-intensive file workloads on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the cloud. Before today, Amazon EFS supported up to 250,000 read IOPS for frequently-accessed data and metadata, and up to 65,000 read IOPS for remaining data and metadata. With this launch, Amazon EFS now supports up to 90,000 read IOPS (a 40% improvement on the existing 65,000 limit), meaning that customers can use Amazon EFS to power an even broader range of IOPS-intensive, read-heavy workloads such as machine learning research, content delivery, and big data processing. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThese higher IOPS limits are immediately available for Amazon EFS file systems using Elastic Throughput, in all commercial AWS Regions and the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-20T17:00:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/01/higher-read-iops-amazon-elastic-file-system/","postDateTime":"2024-01-19T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS announces higher read IOPS for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now delivers 40% higher read IOPS per file system, making it easier to power data-intensive file workloads on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-eds-volume-jupyterlab-codeeditor-amazon-sagemaker-studio","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-eds-volume-jupyterlab-codeeditor-amazon-sagemaker-studio/","dateCreated":"2023-11-30T18:52:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:01:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon SageMaker Studio is a single web-based interface with comprehensive machine learning (ML) tools and a choice of fully managed integrated development environments (IDEs) to perform every step of ML development, from preparing data to building, training, deploying, and managing ML models. Amazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget, elastic file system that makes it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud. Today, we are excited to announce a new capability that allows you to bring you own EFS volume to access your large ML datasets or shared code from IDEs such as JupyterLab and Code Editor in SageMaker Studio.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can now make pre-existing EFS volumes available to multiple users in SageMaker within their IDEs to allow them to access common datasets on a filesystem without requiring data movement thus saving time, effort, and cost.\u003cbr\u003e\r\nWith this, you can also share notebooks, code and data with your colleagues to boost productivity and collaborate faster on your ML workflows. Further, you can access the same EFS volume across different steps of ML workflow such as model building and training enabling you to iterate and experiment quickly.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability is available in all Amazon Web Services (AWS) regions where Amazon SageMaker Studio is currently available, except China and the AWS GovCloud (US) regions. To learn more, please refer to SageMaker Studio \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/domain-custom-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-12-13T20:21:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-eds-volume-jupyterlab-codeeditor-amazon-sagemaker-studio/","postDateTime":"2023-11-30T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Bring your own Amazon EFS (Elastic File System) volume to JupyterLab and CodeEditor in Amazon SageMaker Studio","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon SageMaker Studio is a single web-based interface with comprehensive machine learning (ML) tools and a choice of fully managed integrated development environments (IDEs) to perform every step of ML development, from preparing data to building, training, deploying, and managing ML models. Amazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget, elastic file system that makes it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud. Today, we are excited to announce a new capability that allows you to bring you own EFS volume to access your large ML datasets or shared code from IDEs such as JupyterLab and Code Editor in SageMaker Studio.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-sagemaker-studio","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-sagemaker-studio","description":"general:products/amazon-sagemaker-studio","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:37:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-industry#artificial-intelligence","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-industry","name":"artificial-intelligence","description":"marketing:industry/artificial-intelligence","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:23+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-efs-replication-failback","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-efs-replication-failback/","dateCreated":"2023-11-27T20:11:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:43:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Replication now supports failback, making it easier and more cost-effective to synchronize changes between EFS file systems after Disaster Recovery (DR) and other failover events.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the cloud. Using Amazon EFS Replication, you can maintain an up-to-date secondary copy of your primary file system in the AWS Region of your choice. With this launch, you can now synchronize changes from your secondary file system back to your primary — for example, when performing failback workflows after a DR event – by simply switching the direction of your EFS Replication. EFS will automatically identify and transfer only incremental changes to synchronize your file systems.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEFS Replication failback support is available in all commercial AWS Regions and the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-replication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e and get started by configuring EFS Replication in just a few clicks using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, AWS CLI, AWS CloudFormation, and APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-27T20:11:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-efs-replication-failback/","postDateTime":"2023-11-27T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Replication now supports failback","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Replication now supports failback, making it easier and more cost-effective to synchronize changes between EFS file systems after Disaster Recovery (DR) and other failover events.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-efs-250000-iops-per-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-efs-250000-iops-per-file-system/","dateCreated":"2023-11-26T20:18:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:01:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS now supports up to 250,000 read IOPS and up to 50,000 write IOPS per file system, making it easier to power IOPS-intensive file workloads on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the cloud. Amazon EFS now supports up to 250,000 read IOPS (4.5x improvement) when you are working with frequently-accessed data and up to 50,000 write IOPS (2x improvement). With these IOPS improvements, you can easily run even more demanding workloads on EFS, such as AI/ML (iterative training, fine- tuning, inferencing), data science user shares, SaaS applications, and media processing. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThese higher IOPS limits are immediately available for EFS file systems using Elastic Throughput, in all commercial AWS Regions and the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-26T20:18:09Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-efs-250000-iops-per-file-system/","postDateTime":"2023-11-26T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 250,000 IOPS per file system","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS now supports up to 250,000 read IOPS and up to 50,000 write IOPS per file system, making it easier to power IOPS-intensive file workloads on AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-efs-archive-storage-class","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-efs-archive-storage-class/","dateCreated":"2023-11-26T20:19:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Archive is a new storage class that is cost-optimized for long-lived file data that is accessed a few times a year or less. With EFS Archive, you now have a cost-effective way to retain even your coldest data so that it’s always available to power new business insights. In addition, as part of this launch, the storage price for the existing Amazon EFS Infrequent Access (IA) storage class is being reduced by 36% to make EFS an even better solution for sharing a wide range of data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith EFS Archive, you can now easily and cost-effectively share data for a wide spectrum of use cases – from data analytics to machine learning training to SaaS applications – with the same instant access, gigabytes-per-second throughput, and designed-for 11 9s durability that Amazon EFS delivers today. EFS Archive supports the same intelligent tiering experience as existing EFS storage classes, which means that you can now combine the sub-millisecond SSD latencies of Amazon EFS Standard for your active frequently-accessed data with the lower costs of EFS IA and EFS Archive for your colder data. When needed, all your data is accessible from a single EFS file system that’s automatically cost-optimized for a mix of active and inactive data. With EFS Archive, customers can save up to 50% – compared to the reduced price of EFS IA – when storing long-lived, rarely-accessed data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEFS Archive and the EFS IA price reduction are immediately available for all file systems using the EFS Elastic Throughput mode, in all commercial AWS Regions and the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/optimize-your-storage-costs-for-rarely-accessed-files-with-amazon-efs-archive/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News blog post\u003c/a\u003e, watch the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d2JW6_2CEvcc\u0026amp;t\u003d1s\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eexplainer video\u003c/a\u003e, and read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/storage-classes.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, you can enable Lifecycle Management using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, API, or AWS CLI.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-12-13T21:04:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-efs-archive-storage-class/","postDateTime":"2023-11-26T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing the new Amazon EFS Archive storage class","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Archive is a new storage class that is cost-optimized for long-lived file data that is accessed a few times a year or less. With EFS Archive, you now have a cost-effective way to retain even your coldest data so that it’s always available to power new business insights. In addition, as part of this launch, the storage price for the existing Amazon EFS Infrequent Access (IA) storage class is being reduced by 36% to make EFS an even better solution for sharing a wide range of data.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-efs-aws-israel-tel-aviv-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-efs-aws-israel-tel-aviv-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:40:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-08T17:08:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-efs-aws-israel-tel-aviv-region/","postDateTime":"2023-08-08T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS is now available in the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-efs-55000-iops-per-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-efs-55000-iops-per-file-system/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:08:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:32:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) now supports up to 55,000 read IOPS and 25,000 write IOPS, making it easier to power Machine Learning (ML) research, financial simulations, big data analytics, and other data-intensive workloads on AWS.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the cloud. Amazon EFS now supports up to 55,000 read IOPS per file system, a 1.6x increase, and up to 25,000 write IOPS per file system, a 3.6x increase. With these enhancements, you can easily run more IOPS-demanding workloads on EFS, such as Machine Learning (ML) research with KubeFlow, financial simulations with IBM Symphony, and big data processing with Domino Data Lab, Hadoop, and Spark.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased IOPS limits are immediately available for all Amazon EFS General Purpose file systems using the Elastic Throughput mode or Provisioned Throughput mode, in all AWS regions where EFS is supported. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e or create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, API, or AWS CLI.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-03T17:13:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-efs-55000-iops-per-file-system/","postDateTime":"2023-08-03T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 55,000 IOPS per file system","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) now supports up to 55,000 read IOPS and 25,000 write IOPS, making it easier to power Machine Learning (ML) research, financial simulations, big data analytics, and other data-intensive workloads on AWS.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-eks-configure-efs-shared-file-storage","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-eks-configure-efs-shared-file-storage/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:01:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:52:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) now supports the Amazon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eElastic File System (EFS)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver as an EKS add-on, making it simpler and easier to use EFS shared file storage with your EKS clusters.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe EFS CSI driver provides a container storage interface so that you can attach persistent, fully elastic EFS shared file storage to your Kubernetes clusters running on Amazon EKS. With this launch, Amazon EKS now supports the EFS CSI driver as an EKS add-on, enabling you to install, configure, and update the EFS CSI driver with just a few clicks in the EKS Console, or using the AWS CLI, EKS API, or IAC tools. This capability eliminates the need to manually install and configure the EFS CSI driver using command line tools such as kubectl or helm, and makes it easy to keep your cluster up-to-date with the latest version of this driver: All EKS add-ons, including the EFS CSI driver add-on, automatically include the latest security patches, bug fixes, and are validated by AWS to work with EKS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the EFS CSI driver add-on via the Amazon EKS console, Command Line Interface (CLI), EKS API, and IAC tools in all regions supporting EFS except for AWS China (Beijing) region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) region, operated by NWCD. To learn more and get started,\u0026nbsp;visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EKS documentation on EFS\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-02T17:07:39Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-eks-configure-efs-shared-file-storage/","postDateTime":"2023-08-02T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EKS makes it easier to configure and use Amazon EFS for persistent shared file storage","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) now supports the Amazon \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eElastic File System (EFS)\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver as an EKS add-on, making it simpler and easier to use EFS shared file storage with your EKS clusters.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-efs-up-to-10-gibs-provisioned-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-efs-up-to-10-gibs-provisioned-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:07:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum per file system throughput on Amazon EFS Provisioned Throughput mode by 3x. With this launch, you now have a cost-effective way to drive up to 10 GiB/s of read throughput and 3 GiB/s of write throughput for workloads including machine learning, data processing, analytics, and transcoding that demand consistent and high levels of throughput performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the AWS cloud. Amazon EFS Provisioned Throughput mode offers a cost-effective, predictable way to deliver the required amount of throughput for workloads that consistently drive high levels of throughput performance, including genomics data processing and video transcoding. This launch increases the maximum throughput available on Amazon EFS Provisioned Throughput mode to 10 GiB/s (from 3 GiB/s) of read throughput and 3 GiB/s (from 1 GiB/s) of write throughput; these limits match the maximum throughput available on Elastic Throughput, the throughput mode optimized for unpredictable or spiky workloads such as machine learning inference, analytics user shares, and CI/CD tools.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased throughput limits for Amazon EFS file systems using Provisioned Throughput are available in the US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU West (Dublin) Regions. To learn more, see the EFS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, create a file system using the Amazon EFS Console, API, CDK, CFN, or AWS CLI.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-06-23T21:05:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-efs-up-to-10-gibs-provisioned-throughput/","postDateTime":"2023-06-23T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 10 GiB/s of Provisioned Throughput","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum per file system throughput on Amazon EFS Provisioned Throughput mode by 3x. With this launch, you now have a cost-effective way to drive up to 10 GiB/s of read throughput and 3 GiB/s of write throughput for workloads including machine learning, data processing, analytics, and transcoding that demand consistent and high levels of throughput performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-aws-trusted-advisor-checks-amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/aws-trusted-advisor-checks-amazon-efs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:06:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:48:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Trusted Advisor has launched two checks for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS)\u003c/a\u003e. AWS Trusted Advisor evaluates your AWS account with automated checks and provides cloud optimization recommendations to reduce costs, improve performance, increase security and fault tolerance, and monitor service quotas.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe fault tolerance check for \u003cb\u003eAmazon EFS No Mount Target Redundancy\u003c/b\u003e checks if mount targets exist in multiple Availability Zones. The performance check for \u003cb\u003eAmazon EFS Throughput Mode Optimization\u003c/b\u003e checks to determine if your Amazon EFS file system is not configured to use Elastic, or Provisioned Throughput mode. The checks are available in all commercial Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Premium Support customers can access the fault tolerance checks from the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://console.aws.amazon.com/trustedadvisor/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Trusted Advisor Console\u003c/a\u003e, or via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Support API\u003c/a\u003e. For more information please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/premiumsupport/technology/trusted-advisor/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Trusted Advisor webpage\u003c/a\u003e and the documentation site for a complete list of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/trusted-advisor-check-reference.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003echeck references\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-06-05T18:31:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/aws-trusted-advisor-checks-amazon-efs/","postDateTime":"2023-06-05T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Trusted Advisor adds new checks for Amazon EFS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Trusted Advisor has launched two checks for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS)\u003c/a\u003e. AWS Trusted Advisor evaluates your AWS account with automated checks and provides cloud optimization recommendations to reduce costs, improve performance, increase security and fault tolerance, and monitor service quotas.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-trusted-advisor","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-trusted-advisor","description":"general:products/aws-trusted-advisor","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:58:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-amazon-efs-replication-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-efs-replication-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:59:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) Replication is now available in 10 more AWS Regions: Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad), Asia Pacific (Jakarta), Asia Pacific (Melbourne), Europe (Milan), Europe (Spain), Europe (Zurich), Middle East (Bahrain), Middle East (UAE), in addition to the 19 AWS Regions and 2 AWS GovCloud (US) Regions where it was previously supported. With this launch, EFS Replication is available in all AWS Regions where EFS is supported.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the cloud. Amazon EFS Replication enables you to easily maintain a separate, up-to-date copy of your file system for compliance, localized data access, and testing/development use cases. You can automatically replicate data across AWS Regions, without needing to manually monitor and synchronize data changes. Before today, EFS Replication was available in 19 AWS Regions and 2 AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. Starting today, you can use EFS Replication in 10 additional AWS Regions, allowing you to easily replicate your file data in all AWS Regions where EFS is supported.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-replication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, configure replication for existing file systems in just a few clicks using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, AWS CLI, and APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-05-02T17:00:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-efs-replication-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2023-05-02T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Replication is now available in all AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) Replication is now available in 10 more AWS Regions: Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad), Asia Pacific (Jakarta), Asia Pacific (Melbourne), Europe (Milan), Europe (Spain), Europe (Zurich), Middle East (Bahrain), Middle East (UAE), in addition to the 19 AWS Regions and 2 AWS GovCloud (US) Regions where it was previously supported. With this launch, EFS Replication is available in all AWS Regions where EFS is supported.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-04-amazon-efs-10-gibs-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/04/amazon-efs-10-gibs-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:31:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum throughput per file system by 3x to 10 GiB/s of read throughput and 3 GiB/s of write throughput.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides serverless, fully elastic file storage that makes it simple to set up and run file workloads in the cloud. With these new throughput limits, you can easily run more performance-intensive workloads on AWS using Amazon EFS, such as machine learning, genomics, and data analytics applications.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased throughput limits are immediately available for Amazon EFS file systems using the Elastic Throughput mode in the US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and Europe (Dublin) Regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Documentation\u003c/a\u003e or create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e, API, or AWS CLI.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-04-17T20:01:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/04/amazon-efs-10-gibs-throughput/","postDateTime":"2023-04-17T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports up to 10 GiB/s of throughput","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum throughput per file system by 3x to 10 GiB/s of read throughput and 3 GiB/s of write throughput.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-04-amazon-efs-asia-pacific-melbourne-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/04/amazon-efs-asia-pacific-melbourne-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:39+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Asia Pacific (Melbourne) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-04-12T21:27:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/04/amazon-efs-asia-pacific-melbourne-region/","postDateTime":"2023-04-12T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Melbourne) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Asia Pacific (Melbourne) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-02-amazon-efs-available-aws-asia-pacific-hyderabad-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-efs-available-aws-asia-pacific-hyderabad-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:52:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-02-16T22:05:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-efs-available-aws-asia-pacific-hyderabad-region/","postDateTime":"2023-02-16T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Asia Pacific (Hyderabad) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-01-amazon-efs-aws-europe-spain-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/01/amazon-efs-aws-europe-spain-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:57:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:36:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed to provide serverless, fully elastic file storage that lets you share file data without provisioning or managing storage capacity and performance. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files. Because Amazon EFS has a simple web services interface, you can create and configure file systems quickly and easily. The service is designed to manage file storage infrastructure for you, meaning that you can avoid the complexity of deploying, patching, and maintaining complex file system configurations. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-01-19T22:03:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/01/amazon-efs-aws-europe-spain-region/","postDateTime":"2023-01-19T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Europe (Spain) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Europe (Spain) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-01-amazon-efs-increases-access-points-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/01/amazon-efs-increases-access-points-file-system/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:44:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum number of Access Points per file system from 120 to 1,000, enabling you to control file system access permissions across a larger number of applications in multi-tenant environments.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Access Points are application-specific entry points into your file system which are designed to enforce a specified POSIX identity and root directory for connected clients. You can use EFS Access Points to more easily isolate data between applications sharing a single EFS file system. With this launch, you can now utilize up to 1,000 EFS Access Points per EFS file system for higher scale multi-tenant environments.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased EFS Access Point limit is available for all file systems in all regions supporting EFS, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions, but excluding the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-access-points.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e and create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-04-05T16:50:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/01/amazon-efs-increases-access-points-file-system/","postDateTime":"2023-01-17T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS increases the maximum number of Access Points per file system","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum number of Access Points per file system from 120 to 1,000, enabling you to control file system access permissions across a larger number of applications in multi-tenant environments.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-elastic-file-system-efs-available-aws-europe-zurich-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-elastic-file-system-efs-available-aws-europe-zurich-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:00:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Europe (Zurich) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a serverless, fully elastic file system that is designed to make it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud. It is built to scale on demand to store petabytes of data, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp; product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-15T23:04:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-elastic-file-system-efs-available-aws-europe-zurich-region/","postDateTime":"2022-12-15T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Europe (Zurich) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now create file systems using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the AWS Europe (Zurich) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-aws-announces-lower-latencies-amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-announces-lower-latencies-amazon-elastic-file-system/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:47:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:41:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now delivers lower latencies enabling you to power an even broader set of applications with simple, scalable storage on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS now delivers up to 60% lower read operation latencies when working with frequently-accessed data and metadata. In addition, EFS now delivers up to 40% lower write operation latencies when working with small files (\u0026lt;64 KB) and metadata. Put together, for a typical workload these improvements can benefit the majority of all file operations. With these reductions, in the US East (N. Virginia) Region, for example, read latencies are as low as 0.25 milliseconds for frequently-accessed data, and write latencies are as low as 1.6 milliseconds for EFS-One Zone (and 2.7 milliseconds for EFS-Standard). Applications that may benefit from these improvements include content management systems, analytics, and CI/CD tools.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eLower latencies are available automatically in the US East (N. Virginia) Region for all new EFS file systems using General Purpose performance mode, as well as for new mount targets on existing EFS General Purpose file systems. These enhancements will become available in the remaining AWS commercial regions over the coming weeks. To get started using Amazon EFS, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003csup\u003e\u003cb\u003e12/16/2022\u003c/b\u003e - This post was updated to clarify that latency improvements also apply to new mount targets on existing file systems. Latency improvements are now available in all commercial AWS Regions where Amazon EFS is available\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-16T21:15:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/aws-announces-lower-latencies-amazon-elastic-file-system/","postDateTime":"2022-11-28T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS announces lower latencies for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now delivers lower latencies enabling you to power an even broader set of applications with simple, scalable storage on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-elastic-file-system-1-day-lifecycle-management-policy-reduce-costs-cold-data-sets","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/elastic-file-system-1-day-lifecycle-management-policy-reduce-costs-cold-data-sets/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:51:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports a 1-day Lifecycle Management Policy that allows you to automatically move files that haven’t been accessed in 1 day to the Amazon EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) storage class. You can configure this new policy option for your file system, or you can use one of the existing policy options: 7, 14, 30, 60, or 90 days.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Lifecycle Management enables you to automatically move data stored on the Standard storage class that hasn’t been accessed recently to the cheaper, colder IA storage class, helping you save on storage costs. Applications that ingest and analyze large amounts of data on a daily basis, and then retain the data long-term, can benefit from a 1-day Lifecycle Management policy. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new option for EFS Lifecycle Management is available for all file systems in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon EFS is publicly available. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/whatisefs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e and create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-28T04:41:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/elastic-file-system-1-day-lifecycle-management-policy-reduce-costs-cold-data-sets/","postDateTime":"2022-11-27T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":" Amazon Elastic File System introduces 1-Day Lifecycle Management Policy to help customers reduce costs for cold data sets","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports a 1-day Lifecycle Management Policy that allows you to automatically move files that haven’t been accessed in 1 day to the Amazon EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) storage class. You can configure this new policy option for your file system, or you can use one of the existing policy options: 7, 14, 30, 60, or 90 days.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-elastic-file-system-elastic-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-elastic-file-system-elastic-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:58:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eElastic Throughput is a new throughput mode for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) that is designed to provide your applications with as much throughput as they need with pay-as-you-use pricing. Elastic Throughput is designed to further simplify running workloads and applications on AWS by providing file storage that doesn’t require any performance provisioning.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eElastic Throughput is ideal for spiky and unpredictable workloads with performance requirements that are difficult to forecast. When you enable Elastic Throughput on an EFS file system, you don’t specify or provision throughput capacity to meet your application needs; instead, with Elastic Throughput, EFS is designed to automatically deliver the throughput performance your application needs while you pay only for the amount of data read or written.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS already provides fully elastic, pay-as-you-use storage. With Elastic Throughput, Amazon EFS now extends its simplicity and elasticity to performance, so you don’t have to think about provisioning or planning any resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Elastic Throughput is available in all regions supporting EFS except for AWS China (Beijing) region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) region, operated by NWCD. To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-announcing-amazon-efs-elastic-throughput/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News Blog\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/managing-throughput.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, configure Elastic Throughput for existing and new file systems in just a few clicks using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-01-09T20:37:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-elastic-file-system-elastic-throughput/","postDateTime":"2022-11-27T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing Elastic Throughput for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eElastic Throughput is a new throughput mode for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) that is designed to provide your applications with as much throughput as they need with pay-as-you-use pricing. Elastic Throughput is designed to further simplify running workloads and applications on AWS by providing file storage that doesn’t require any performance provisioning.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-10-amazon-elastic-file-system-available-middle-east-uae-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/amazon-elastic-file-system-available-middle-east-uae-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:28:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Middle East (UAE) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a serverless, fully elastic file system that makes it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud.  It is built to scale on demand to store petabytes of data, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-10-18T22:14:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/amazon-elastic-file-system-available-middle-east-uae-region/","postDateTime":"2022-10-18T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Middle East (UAE) region.","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Middle East (UAE) Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-amazon-efs-larger-number-concurrent-file-locks","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-efs-larger-number-concurrent-file-locks/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:21:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum number of file locks per NFS mount, enabling customers to use the service for a broader set of workloads that leverage high volumes of simultaneous locks, including message brokers and distributed analytics applications. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a serverless, fully elastic file system that makes it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud. It can be accessed from any AWS compute service (including Amazon EC2, Amazon EKS, Amazon ECS, and AWS Lambda), and it supports access from up to tens of thousands of compute instances, containers, and function invocations at the same time. Applications spanning multiple compute resources commonly use NFS file locks to manage concurrent updates to individual files. This Amazon EFS update increases the number of simultaneous file locks an NFS mount can acquire to 65,536 (from 8,192 previously), enabling Amazon EFS to be used for a broader set of applications that heavily leverage file locking (including message broker and distributed analytics applications).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased per mount lock limits are available for existing and new file systems in all public \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;where Amazon EFS is available with no action required. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/whatisefs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and create a file system using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-10T17:14:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-efs-larger-number-concurrent-file-locks/","postDateTime":"2022-05-10T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports a larger number of concurrent file locks","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) has increased the maximum number of file locks per NFS mount, enabling customers to use the service for a broader set of workloads that leverage high volumes of simultaneous locks, including message brokers and distributed analytics applications. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-aws-lambda-support-amazon-elastic-file-system-available-asia-pacific-jakarta-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/aws-lambda-support-amazon-elastic-file-system-available-asia-pacific-jakarta-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:56:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Lambda customers can now enable functions to access Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region. With AWS Lambda support for Amazon EFS, customers can easily share data across function invocations, read large reference data files, and write function output to a persistent and shared data store.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can use AWS Lambda with Amazon EFS to build data-intensive applications, load larger libraries and models, process larger amounts of data in a highly distributed manner, and share data across functions, containers, and instances. AWS Lambda will automatically mount the file system and provide a local path to read and write data at low latency.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on availability, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region table\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, view our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-05T22:11:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/aws-lambda-support-amazon-elastic-file-system-available-asia-pacific-jakarta-region/","postDateTime":"2022-05-05T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Lambda support for Amazon Elastic File System now available in Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Lambda customers can now enable functions to access Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) in the Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region. With AWS Lambda support for Amazon EFS, customers can easily share data across function invocations, read large reference data files, and write function output to a persistent and shared data store.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-lambda","description":"general:products/aws-lambda","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-02-sub-millisecond-read-latencies-amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/02/sub-millisecond-read-latencies-amazon-elastic-file-system/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:16:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports sub-millisecond read latencies for all new and existing One Zone and Standard General Purpose file systems. Latency-sensitive applications such as content management systems, analytics, DevOps, and machine learning inference can now achieve read latencies as low as 600 microseconds on average.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget, elastic file system that makes it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud. It is built to scale on demand to store petabytes of data without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth. Amazon EFS can elastically scale to be consumed from tens of thousands of connections from any AWS compute including Amazon EC2 instances, serverless functions, and containers.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eSub-millisecond read latencies are available in all AWS Regions where Amazon EFS is available with no action required.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-elastic-file-system-update-sub-millisecond-read-latency/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News blog post\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ethe EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and create a file system in a single-click using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-02-14T22:51:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/02/sub-millisecond-read-latencies-amazon-elastic-file-system/","postDateTime":"2022-02-14T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing sub-millisecond read latencies for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports sub-millisecond read latencies for all new and existing One Zone and Standard General Purpose file systems. Latency-sensitive applications such as content management systems, analytics, DevOps, and machine learning inference can now achieve read latencies as low as 600 microseconds on average.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-new-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-new-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:06:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget, elastic file system that makes it easy to set up, scale, and cost-optimize file storage in the AWS Cloud. It is built to scale on demand to store petabytes of data without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-27T22:59:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-new-region/","postDateTime":"2022-01-27T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the AWS Asia Pacific (Jakarta) Region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-amazon-elastic-file-system-replication","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-replication/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:10:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Replication provides you with an easy way to keep an up-to-date copy of your file system in a second AWS Region or within the same Region. Amazon EFS Replication enables you to replicate file data in a few clicks and without requiring you to manually provision additional infrastructure or a custom process to monitor and synchronize data changes. Amazon EFS Replication is designed to meet a recovery point objective (RPO) and recovery time objective (RTO) of minutes, enabling you to meet your business continuity and compliance requirements.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, serverless, set-and-forget, elastic file system for use with AWS services and on-premises resources. It offers you the choice of Standard storage classes, which are designed to store data within a minimum of three Availability Zones (AZs), each separated by miles within an AWS Region for higher availability and higher durability, and One Zone storage classes, which are designed to store data in a single AZ.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed for 99.999999999% (11 9’s) of durability and high availability. However, organizations in regulated industries are often subject to compliance requirements that mandate storing secondary data copies several hundred miles away from the original. You can use Amazon EFS Replication to automatically maintain a copy of your Amazon EFS file system in a Region or AZ of  your choice, using the Amazon EFS console, AWS CLI, and APIs to enable replication on an existing file system.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Replication is available in AWS US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon), Asia Paciﬁc (Mumbai), Asia Paciﬁc (Osaka), Asia Paciﬁc (Seoul), Asia Paciﬁc (Singapore), Asia Paciﬁc (Sydney), Asia Paciﬁc (Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Europe (Stockholm), South America (São Paulo), and AWS GovCloud (US). To learn more, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-replication-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News Blog\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-replication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, configure replication for existing file systems in just a few clicks using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-25T23:19:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-replication/","postDateTime":"2022-01-25T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing Amazon Elastic File System Replication","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Replication provides you with an easy way to keep an up-to-date copy of your file system in a second AWS Region or within the same Region. Amazon EFS Replication enables you to replicate file data in a few clicks and without requiring you to manually provision additional infrastructure or a custom process to monitor and synchronize data changes. Amazon EFS Replication is designed to meet a recovery point objective (RPO) and recovery time objective (RTO) of minutes, enabling you to meet your business continuity and compliance requirements.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-09-amazon-elastic-file-system-intelligent-tiering","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/amazon-elastic-file-system-intelligent-tiering/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:14:04+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) now supports Intelligent-Tiering, a new capability that makes it easier for you to optimize costs for shared file storage, even when access patterns change. EFS Intelligent-Tiering is designed to help you achieve the right price and performance blend for your application file data by placing your file data in a storage class based on file access patterns.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eEFS Intelligent-Tiering uses Lifecycle Management to monitor the access patterns of your workload and is designed to automatically transition files that are not accessed for the duration of the Lifecycle policy (e.g. 30 days) from either the EFS Standard or EFS One Zone storage classes, to their corresponding Infrequent Access (IA) storage class (EFS Standard-Infrequent Access or EFS One Zone-Infrequent Access). This helps you take advantage of IA storage pricing that is up to 92% lower than the EFS Standard or EFS One Zone file storage pricing for workloads with changing access patterns.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, if access patterns change, EFS Intelligent-Tiering is designed to automatically move files back to performance-optimized (EFS Standard or EFS One Zone) storage classes. This helps you eliminate the risk of unbounded access charges, while providing consistent low latencies. If the files become infrequently accessed again, EFS Intelligent-Tiering is designed to transition the files back to IA based on your Lifecycle policy.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Intelligent-Tiering is available in all AWS regions where Amazon EFS is available.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-amazon-efs-intelligent-tiering-optimizes-costs-for-workloads-with-changing-access-patterns\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News blog\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/lifecycle-management-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and create a file system in a single-click using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-02T15:50:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/09/amazon-elastic-file-system-intelligent-tiering/","postDateTime":"2021-09-02T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System introduces Intelligent-Tiering to automatically optimize storage costs","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) now supports Intelligent-Tiering, a new capability that makes it easier for you to optimize costs for shared file storage, even when access patterns change. EFS Intelligent-Tiering is designed to help you achieve the right price and performance blend for your application file data by placing your file data in a storage class based on file access patterns.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-07-aws-solutions-implementation-simple-file-manager-amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/aws-solutions-implementation-simple-file-manager-amazon-efs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are launching \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/simple-file-manager-for-amazon-efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSimple File Manager for Amazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementations portfolio\u003c/a\u003e. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/simple-file-manager-for-amazon-efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSimple File Manager for Amazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e is a serverless solution that provides a user interface for managing data in your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) file systems. Deploying this solution allows you to seamlessly browse any EFS file system in your Amazon Web Services, Inc. (AWS) account and upload, download, or delete data from virtually any device, without the need to setup or maintain any dedicated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Compute Cloud\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EC2) or networking infrastructure. As an example, you can use this solution to upload large machine learning (ML) model files to an Amazon EFS file system that is used by an AWS Lambda function for ML inference.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with the solution, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/simple-file-manager-for-amazon-efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solution Library\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-efs-simple-file-manager\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e. AWS Solutions Implementations help you solve common problems and build faster using the AWS platform. Additional AWS Solutions Implementations are available on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethe AWS Solutions Implementations webpage\u003c/a\u003e, where you can browse technical reference implementations that are vetted by AWS architects, offering detailed architecture and instructions for deployment to help build faster and solve common problems.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-07-15T22:54:49Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/07/aws-solutions-implementation-simple-file-manager-amazon-efs/","postDateTime":"2021-07-15T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New AWS Solutions Implementation: Simple File Manager for Amazon EFS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are launching \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations/simple-file-manager-for-amazon-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSimple File Manager for Amazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e into the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementations portfolio\u003c/a\u003e. \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations/simple-file-manager-for-amazon-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSimple File Manager for Amazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e is a serverless solution that provides a user interface for managing data in your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) file systems. Deploying this solution allows you to seamlessly browse any EFS file system in your Amazon Web Services, Inc. (AWS) account and upload, download, or delete data from virtually any device, without the need to setup or maintain any dedicated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/ec2.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Compute Cloud\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EC2) or networking infrastructure. As an example, you can use this solution to upload large machine learning (ML) model files to an Amazon EFS file system that is used by an AWS Lambda function for ML inference.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-06-easily-install-and-manage-amazon-efs-utilities-on-your-instances-with-quick-setup","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/easily-install-and-manage-amazon-efs-utilities-on-your-instances-with-quick-setup/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:08:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Systems Manager Quick Setup announces support for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), enabling you to set up Amazon EFS client (amazon-efs-utils) across all the Amazon EC2 instances in your organization with a few clicks. In addition to installing and configuring the Amazon EFS client, Quick Setup also supports periodically updating the client to the latest available version.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon EFS client includes a mount helper and tooling that makes it easier to perform encryption of data in transit for Amazon EFS file systems. With Systems Manager Quick Setup, you can automatically configure and update the Amazon EFS client on all the instances across the accounts and Regions in your organization.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, choose Quick Setup from the Systems Manager left navigation menu. Systems Manager Quick Setup support for AWS Organizations is available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), and South America (São Paulo) AWS Regions. For more information about Quick Setup, visit the AWS Systems Manager \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-quick-setup.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-06-09T16:59:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/06/easily-install-and-manage-amazon-efs-utilities-on-your-instances-with-quick-setup/","postDateTime":"2021-06-09T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Easily install and manage Amazon EFS utilities on your instances with Quick Setup","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, AWS Systems Manager Quick Setup announces support for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), enabling you to set up Amazon EFS client (amazon-efs-utils) across all the Amazon EC2 instances in your organization with a few clicks. In addition to installing and configuring the Amazon EFS client, Quick Setup also supports periodically updating the client to the latest available version.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-tools","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-tools","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-tools","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-amazon-elastic-file-system-supports-longer-resource-identifiers","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/amazon-elastic-file-system-supports-longer-resource-identifiers/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:45:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) will support the use of longer resource identifiers (IDs) for newly created file systems and mount targets. You can opt into this change by using the API, Command Line Interface (CLI), Cloud Development Kit (CDK), and Amazon EFS Console.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFrom now until the end of September 2021, you can test your workloads with the longer format and opt in when you are ready. After September 2021, all new resources will be created with longer IDs by default. Note that the new format will only apply to newly created resources; your existing resources won\u0027t be affected. We strongly recommend testing your systems and opting in to the longer ID format across all of your accounts before the end of September 2021.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe current format is a resource identifier followed by an 8-character string. The new format will be the same resource identifier followed by a 17-character string. For example, today, your file system has a resource identifier like “fs-1234abc0”. After September 2021, a new file system will be assigned an identifier like “fs-1234567890abcdef0”.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis change is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e. For more information please refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-efs-resource-ids.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-21T21:11:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/amazon-elastic-file-system-supports-longer-resource-identifiers/","postDateTime":"2021-05-21T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System now supports longer resource identifiers","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) will support the use of longer resource identifiers (IDs) for newly created file systems and mount targets. You can opt into this change by using the API, Command Line Interface (CLI), Cloud Development Kit (CDK), and Amazon EFS Console.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-aws-backup-now-supports-cost-allocation-tags-for-amazon-efs-backups","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/aws-backup-now-supports-cost-allocation-tags-for-amazon-efs-backups/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to use cost allocation tags for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e backups within \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/aws-cost-management/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Billing and Cost Management\u003c/a\u003e. With cost allocation tags, you can get better transparency and visibility into your Amazon EFS backup costs. For example, you can allocate your Amazon EFS backup costs to different departments (e.g., finance, engineering) or analyze Amazon EFS backup costs across your various workloads to better understand and manage your costs.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup enables you to centralize and automate data protection across AWS services, support your regulatory compliance obligations, and meet your business continuity goals. Amazon EFS backups created through AWS Backup automatically inherit tags from underlying Amazon EFS file systems. You can \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/editing-a-backup.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eedit tags\u003c/a\u003e on your existing Amazon EFS backups using AWS Backup. Now, once you have assigned tags to your Amazon EFS backups, you can visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/billing/home?#/preferences/tags\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Billing and Cost Management dashboard\u003c/a\u003e to activate cost allocation tags for reporting in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/aws-cost-management/aws-cost-explorer/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Cost Explorer\u003c/a\u003e. For more information, visit the documentation regarding \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-alloc-tags.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eusing cost allocation tags\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\nThis feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions where AWS Backup is available\u003c/a\u003e at no additional cost. To learn more about AWS Backup, visit the AWS Backup \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup console\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003cbr\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-07T18:25:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/aws-backup-now-supports-cost-allocation-tags-for-amazon-efs-backups/","postDateTime":"2021-04-07T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Backup now supports cost allocation tags for Amazon EFS Backups","postSummary":"\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/backup.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to use cost allocation tags for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e backups within \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/aws-cost-management.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Billing and Cost Management\u003c/a\u003e. With cost allocation tags, you can get better transparency and visibility into your Amazon EFS backup costs. For example, you can allocate your Amazon EFS backup costs to different departments (e.g., finance, engineering) or analyze Amazon EFS backup costs across your various workloads to better understand and manage your costs.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-backup","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-backup","description":"general:products/aws-backup","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#cost-management","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"cost-management","description":"marketing:marchitecture/cost-management","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:11+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-are-now-available-in-asia-osaka-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-are-now-available-in-asia-osaka-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:52:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e One Zone is now available in the Asia (Osaka) Region, reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the Amazon EFS capabilities that customers love.  \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\nAmazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget elastic file system for use with AWS cloud services and on-premises resources, and is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications. With Amazon EFS, you can grow and shrink your file systems automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith this launch EFS One Zone is now available in all regions where EFS is available.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS News blog\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e and try it out using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-25T21:53:28Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-are-now-available-in-asia-osaka-region/","postDateTime":"2021-03-25T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Lower Cost Storage Classes for Amazon Elastic File System are now available in Asia (Osaka) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e One Zone is now available in the Asia (Osaka) Region, reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the Amazon EFS capabilities that customers love.  \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-amazon-efs-csi-driver-supports-dynamic-provisioning","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-efs-csi-driver-supports-dynamic-provisioning/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:40:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver now supports dynamic provisioning of Kubernetes persistent volumes. Kubernetes applications requiring access to a shared file system on AWS can now have storage provisioned on demand, eliminating the need for cluster administrators to pre-provision volumes.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe EFS CSI driver makes it simple to configure elastic file storage for both EKS and self-managed Kubernetes clusters running on AWS using standard Kubernetes interfaces. Applications running in Kubernetes can use EFS file systems to share data between pods in a scale-out group, or with other applications running within or outside of Kubernetes. Applications can also use Amazon EFS to persist data at a regional level, allowing pods to failover between Availability Zones. Dynamic provisioning in the EFS CSI driver leverages EFS access points, application-specific entry points into an EFS file system that make it easier to share a file system between multiple pods. Each access point created by the CSI driver enforces a unique identity and root directory to ensure application data is private to a persistent volume.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html\"\u003eEKS documentation\u003c/a\u003e or the open source EFS CSI driver project on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-efs-csi-driver\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e. You can also learn more in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/containers/introducing-efs-csi-dynamic-provisioning\"\u003elaunch blog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-23T18:19:28Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-efs-csi-driver-supports-dynamic-provisioning/","postDateTime":"2021-03-23T18:49:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS CSI driver now supports dynamic provisioning","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver now supports dynamic provisioning of Kubernetes persistent volumes. Kubernetes applications requiring access to a shared file system on AWS can now have storage provisioned on demand, eliminating the need for cluster administrators to pre-provision volumes.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-file-system","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-file-system","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-are-now-available-in-additional-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-are-now-available-in-additional-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:57:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) One Zone is now available in 5 additional regions, reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the Amazon EFS capabilities that customers love. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget elastic file system for use with AWS cloud services and on-premises resources, and is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications. With Amazon EFS, you can grow and shrink your file systems automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eToday’s launch adds Europe (London) Region, Europe (Paris) Region, Canada (Central) Region, China (Beijing) Region operated by Beijing Sinnet Technology Co., Ltd., and China (Ningxia) Region operated by Ningxia Western Cloud Data Technology Co., Ltd. to the list of regions where Amazon EFS One Zone is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/introducing-lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ealready available\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS News blog,\u003c/a\u003e the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e and try it out using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-16T17:34:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-are-now-available-in-additional-regions/","postDateTime":"2021-03-16T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Lower Cost Storage Classes for Amazon Elastic File System are now available in additional regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) One Zone is now available in 5 additional regions, reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the Amazon EFS capabilities that customers love. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-introducing-amazon-elastic-file-system-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/introducing-amazon-elastic-file-system-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:02:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports single Availability Zone (AZ) storage classes (One Zone), reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the EFS capabilities that customers love. With this launch, you can achieve an effective storage price of $0.043/GB-month.[1]\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon EFS One Zone, you have the choice of a simple, serverless, set-and-forget elastic file system in a single AZ at 47% lower cost than Amazon EFS Standard. Amazon EFS One Zone is ideal for workloads such as development, build, and staging environments, as well as applications such as analytics, simulation and media transcoding, and for backups or replicas of on-premises data which do not require regional resilience. Amazon EFS is designed for 99.999999999% (11 9’s) durability, and all file systems using One Zone storage classes have automatic backup policies to provide additional data protection with regional redundancy.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS One Zone storage classes are available in US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Milan), Europe (Stockholm), South America (Sao Paulo), Africa (Cape Town), Middle East (Bahrain), and all AWS GovCloud (US) regions, with more regions coming soon.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS News blog\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, and try it out using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e[1] pricing in US-East (Northern Virginia) Region, assumes you are using Lifecycle Management and 80% of your storage is in EFS IA.\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-11T18:13:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/introducing-amazon-elastic-file-system-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes/","postDateTime":"2021-03-09T18:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Lower Cost Storage Classes for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports single Availability Zone (AZ) storage classes (One Zone), reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the EFS capabilities that customers love. With this launch, you can achieve an effective storage price of $0.043/GB-month.[1]\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-introducing-lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/introducing-lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:40:11+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports single Availability Zone (AZ) storage classes (One Zone), reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the EFS capabilities that customers love. With this launch, you can achieve an effective storage price of $0.043/GB-month.[1]\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon EFS One Zone, you have the choice of a simple, serverless, set-and-forget elastic file system in a single AZ at 47% lower cost than Amazon EFS Standard. Amazon EFS One Zone is ideal for workloads such as development, build, and staging environments, as well as applications such as analytics, simulation and media transcoding, and for backups or replicas of on-premises data which do not require regional resilience. Amazon EFS is designed for 99.999999999% (11 9’s) durability, and all file systems using One Zone storage classes have automatic backup policies to provide additional data protection with regional redundancy.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS One Zone storage classes are available in US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (Milan), Europe (Stockholm), South America (Sao Paulo), Africa (Cape Town), Middle East (Bahrain), and all AWS GovCloud (US) regions, with more regions coming soon.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-lower-cost-one-zone-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS News blog\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, and try it out using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e[1] pricing in US-East (Northern Virginia) Region, assumes you are using Lifecycle Management and 80% of your storage is in EFS IA.\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-09T22:10:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/introducing-lower-cost-storage-classes-for-amazon-elastic-file-system/","postDateTime":"2021-03-09T18:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Lower Cost Storage Classes for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports single Availability Zone (AZ) storage classes (One Zone), reducing storage costs by 47% compared to Amazon EFS Standard storage classes, while maintaining the EFS capabilities that customers love. With this launch, you can achieve an effective storage price of $0.043/GB-month.[1]\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-amazon-elastic-file-system-available-aws-osaka-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-available-aws-osaka-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:11:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the\u0026nbsp;AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a simple, serverless, set-and-forget elastic file system\u0026nbsp;for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-03-03T21:56:42Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-available-aws-osaka-region/","postDateTime":"2021-03-03T21:23:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the\u0026nbsp;AWS Asia Pacific (Osaka) Region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-file-system","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-file-system","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-02-simplified-amazon-elastic-file-system-management-console-available-aws-govcloud-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/02/simplified-amazon-elastic-file-system-management-console-available-aws-govcloud-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:10:36+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: left;\"\u003eYou can now use the updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.  The updated console makes it even easier for you to create and manage your file system resources. In addition to a refreshed look and feel, you can create file systems configured with the recommended settings in just few clicks. You can also monitor your file system’s behavior using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e metrics and alarms natively in the Amazon EFS console.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor monitoring, you can now view Amazon CloudWatch alarms you have configured for your Amazon EFS file system metrics in the Amazon EFS console. The console now includes a dashboard that uses\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/using-metric-math.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Metric Math\u003c/a\u003e to display throughput, storage, and IOPS utilization along with other Amazon EFS metrics, enabling you to understand your file system’s behavior against its limits and take actions as needed. \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe updated Amazon EFS console is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall commercial AWS regions\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) regions\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more by reading our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/storage/making-it-even-simpler-to-get-started-with-amazon-efs/\"\u003eblog about the updated Amazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/index.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and log into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e to get started.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-02-17T17:57:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/02/simplified-amazon-elastic-file-system-management-console-available-aws-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2021-02-17T19:13:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplified Amazon Elastic File System management console now available in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: left;\"\u003eYou can now use the updated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.  The updated console makes it even easier for you to create and manage your file system resources. In addition to a refreshed look and feel, you can create file systems configured with the recommended settings in just few clicks. You can also monitor your file system’s behavior using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudwatch.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e metrics and alarms natively in the Amazon EFS console.\u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-01-amazon-elastic-file-system-triples-read-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-triples-read-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:53:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now allows you to drive up to 3x higher read throughput on your file system. For example, bursting mode file systems now provide 300MB/s of bursting read throughput, or 300MB/s per TiB of data stored in Amazon EFS standard, whichever is higher. If you have configured 1 GB/s of provisioned throughput, your application can now drive up to 3 GB/s for read operations (and continue to drive 1GB/s for write operations) without any application or configuration changes. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable, serverless file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. The new increased read throughput improves performance of most applications running on Amazon EFS, especially read-heavy workloads like web serving and machine learning (ML), which are commonly deployed in containers using Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) and Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), and functions using AWS Lambda. This increased read throughput allows real-time applications like ML inference to handle 3x more concurrent requests, and ML model training jobs to complete up to 3x faster.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe throughput increase is automatically enabled for all file systems at no additional cost in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e including the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e, the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD. For more information about Amazon EFS performance, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-01-29T18:04:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-triples-read-throughput/","postDateTime":"2021-01-29T21:59:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System triples read throughput","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now allows you to drive up to 3x higher read throughput on your file system. For example, bursting mode file systems now provide 300MB/s of bursting read throughput, or 300MB/s per TiB of data stored in Amazon EFS standard, whichever is higher. If you have configured 1 GB/s of provisioned throughput, your application can now drive up to 3 GB/s for read operations (and continue to drive 1GB/s for write operations) without any application or configuration changes. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-01-monitor-your-amazon-efs-storage-usage-with-amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/monitor-your-amazon-efs-storage-usage-with-amazon-cloudwatch/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:24:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now monitor the storage size of your Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) resources using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e. Using the Amazon EFS or Amazon CloudWatch consoles, you can view your file system\u0027s storage size over time, including size in each of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/storage-classes.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS storage classes\u003c/a\u003e - EFS Standard, and the cost-optimized EFS Infrequent Access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, log into your Amazon EFS console, select a file system, and navigate to the ‘Monitoring’ tab. Here, you can view a graph for the StorageBytes metric, which displays your file system\u0027s storage size for each storage class. The metric is also available to monitor from the CloudWatch console and its API, CLI, and the AWS SDKs. The breakdown of usage by storage class helps you understand how \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/lifecycle-management-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS lifecycle management\u003c/a\u003e can reduce storage costs over time as it moves your files from EFS Standard to EFS Infrequent Access.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new metric is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e and can be viewed using the EFS console in all AWS commercial regions. You can learn more by logging into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e and by reading the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2021-01-11T22:52:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/monitor-your-amazon-efs-storage-usage-with-amazon-cloudwatch/","postDateTime":"2021-01-11T12:36:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Monitor your Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) storage usage with Amazon CloudWatch","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now monitor the storage size of your Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) resources using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudwatch.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e. Using the Amazon EFS or Amazon CloudWatch consoles, you can view your file system\u0027s storage size over time, including size in each of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/storage-classes.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS storage classes\u003c/a\u003e - EFS Standard, and the cost-optimized EFS Infrequent Access.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-01-introducing-aws-transfer-family-support-for-amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/introducing-aws-transfer-family-support-for-amazon-efs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sftp/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Transfer Family\u003c/a\u003e now supports file transfers for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file systems, enabling AWS Transfer Family customers to easily and securely provide their business partners and end customers access to files stored in Amazon EFS file systems for use cases such as data distribution, supply chain workflows, content management, and web serving applications. With this launch, you can use AWS Transfer Family and Amazon EFS to migrate your file transfer workflows that rely on file storage without impacting your end users or application integrations, while eliminating the need to manage any file transfer infrastructure.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Transfer Family has provided fully managed support for serverless file transfers to and from Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) since the service launched in 2018. With today\u0027s launch, AWS Transfer Family now also supports Amazon EFS enabling you to simplify and accelerate migration of file transfer workflows to AWS. Amazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic file system for use with AWS services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth. When you select Amazon EFS as the data store for your AWS Transfer Family server, files transferred over Secure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP), File Transfer Protocol (FTP) and FTP over SSL (FTPS) will be stored in your Amazon EFS file systems. The transferred files are readily available to your business-critical applications running on Amazon EC2, as well as to containerized and serverless applications run using AWS services such as Amazon ECS, Amazon EKS, AWS Fargate, and AWS Lambda.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions where AWS Transfer Family is available\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, learn more by visiting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-aws-transfer-family-support-for-amazon-elastic-file-system/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS News launch blog\u003c/a\u003e, AWS Transfer Family \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/aws-transfer-family/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/transfer/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e, or sign in to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://us-west-1.console.aws.amazon.com/transfer/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Transfer Family console\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2021-01-07T20:26:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/introducing-aws-transfer-family-support-for-amazon-efs/","postDateTime":"2021-01-07T11:34:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing AWS Transfer Family support for Amazon Elastic File System","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/sftp.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Transfer Family\u003c/a\u003e now supports file transfers for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file systems, enabling AWS Transfer Family customers to easily and securely provide their business partners and end customers access to files stored in Amazon EFS file systems for use cases such as data distribution, supply chain workflows, content management, and web serving applications. With this launch, you can use AWS Transfer Family and Amazon EFS to migrate your file transfer workflows that rely on file storage without impacting your end users or application integrations, while eliminating the need to manage any file transfer infrastructure.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"migration","description":"marketing:marchitecture/migration","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-transfer-family","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-transfer-family","description":"general:products/aws-transfer-family","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-automatic-backups-amazon-elastic-file-system-aws-backup-aws-europe-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/automatic-backups-amazon-elastic-file-system-aws-backup-aws-europe-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now take automatic backups of your Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file systems with AWS Backup in AWS Europe (Milan) and AWS Africa (Cape Town) regions, directly using the Amazon EFS console or API. Automatic backups for Amazon EFS further simplifies backup management of your file systems by enabling you to meet your business and regulatory backup compliance requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e offers a centralized, fully-managed, and policy-based service to protect customer data and ensure compliance across AWS services for business continuity purposes. With AWS Backup, you can centrally configure data protection (backup) policies and monitor backup activity across your AWS resources, including Amazon EBS volumes, Amazon Relational Database Service (RDS) databases (including Aurora clusters), Amazon DynamoDB tables, Amazon Elastic File System (EFS), Amazon EC2 instances, and AWS Storage Gateway volumes.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAutomatic backups for Amazon EFS is available in all regions where AWS Backup is available. You can learn more by reading the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product pages and documentation, and logging into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e to get started. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-11T21:31:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/automatic-backups-amazon-elastic-file-system-aws-backup-aws-europe-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-11-11T12:03:21Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Automatic backups for Amazon Elastic File System using AWS Backup is now available in AWS Europe (Milan) and AWS Africa (Cape Town) regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now take automatic backups of your Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file systems with AWS Backup in AWS Europe (Milan) and AWS Africa (Cape Town) regions, directly using the Amazon EFS console or API. Automatic backups for Amazon EFS further simplifies backup management of your file systems by enabling you to meet your business and regulatory backup compliance requirements. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-backup","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-backup","description":"general:products/aws-backup","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-simplified-amazon-elastic-file-system-management-console-available-milan-cape-town-china-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/simplified-amazon-elastic-file-system-management-console-available-milan-cape-town-china-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS Europe (Milan), AWS Africa (Cape Town), AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by Ningxia Western Cloud Data Technology Co., Ltd. (“NWCD”) and the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Beijing Sinnet Technology Co., Ltd. (“Sinnet”).  The updated console makes it even easier for you to create and manage your file system resources. In addition to a refreshed look and feel, you can create file systems configured with the recommended settings in just a few clicks and you can customize your view to quickly find information you’re looking for.   You can also monitor your file system’s behavior using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e metrics and alarms natively in the Amazon EFS console.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor monitoring, any Amazon CloudWatch alarms you have configured for your Amazon EFS file system metrics will be displayed in the Amazon EFS console. The console now includes a dashboard that uses \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/using-metric-math.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/using-metric-math.html\"\u003eMetric Math\u003c/a\u003e to display throughput and IOPS utilization along with other Amazon EFS metrics, enabling you to understand your file system’s behavior against its limits and take action, if required. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe updated Amazon EFS console is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall commercial AWS regions\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more by reading our blog about the updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/storage/making-it-even-simpler-to-get-started-with-amazon-efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/index.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and log into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e to get started.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-11T21:19:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/simplified-amazon-elastic-file-system-management-console-available-milan-cape-town-china-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-11-11T10:50:15Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplified Amazon Elastic File System management console now available in AWS Europe (Milan), AWS Africa (Cape Town) and AWS China regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the updated \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS Europe (Milan), AWS Africa (Cape Town), AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by Ningxia Western Cloud Data Technology Co., Ltd. (“NWCD”) and the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Beijing Sinnet Technology Co., Ltd. (“Sinnet”).  The updated console makes it even easier for you to create and manage your file system resources. In addition to a refreshed look and feel, you can create file systems configured with the recommended settings in just a few clicks and you can customize your view to quickly find information you’re looking for.   You can also monitor your file system’s behavior using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudwatch.html\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch\u003c/a\u003e metrics and alarms natively in the Amazon EFS console.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-quickly-create-amazon-efs-file-systems-ec2-launch-instance-wizard","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/quickly-create-amazon-efs-file-systems-ec2-launch-instance-wizard/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:06:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Quick Create from the Amazon EC2 Launch Instance Wizard to create new file systems using the recommended settings without having to leave the Amazon EC2 console. You can then immediately add your newly created file system to the EC2 instance you are launching and it will be automatically mounted on your instance after it has launched. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e provides a simple, scalable, cloud native, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth. Amazon EFS is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Quick Create for the Amazon EC2 Launch Instance Wizard is available at no additional charge in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, open the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/v2/home?#LaunchInstanceWizard:\"\u003eEC2 Launch Instance Wizard\u003c/a\u003e and click on “Create new file system” in \u003cb\u003eStep 3: Configure Instance Details\u003c/b\u003e. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/launching-instance.html\"\u003eEC2 Launch Instance Wizard documentation\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/whatisefs.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-09T18:47:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/quickly-create-amazon-efs-file-systems-ec2-launch-instance-wizard/","postDateTime":"2020-11-09T11:37:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Quickly create Amazon EFS file systems from the EC2 Launch Instance Wizard","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Quick Create from the Amazon EC2 Launch Instance Wizard to create new file systems using the recommended settings without having to leave the Amazon EC2 console. You can then immediately add your newly created file system to the EC2 instance you are launching and it will be automatically mounted on your instance after it has launched. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage-day","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage-day","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage-day","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:24+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-amazon-efs-integrates-aws-systems-manager-simplify-management-amazon-efs-clients","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-efs-integrates-aws-systems-manager-simplify-management-amazon-efs-clients/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) integrates with AWS Systems Manager to simplify management of Amazon EFS clients. You can now use AWS Systems Manager to automate the tasks required to install the latest version of the Amazon EFS client (amazon-efs-utils) package on your Amazon EC2 instances maintaining compliance and security by ensuring that the Amazon EFS client is kept up to date. Additionally, you can orchestrate file system mounts to multiple instances using a single command and improve visibility by monitoring the file system mount status using CloudWatch Logs. You do not need to login to your Amazon EC2 instances to manage your Amazon EFS clients.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e provides a simple, scalable, cloud native, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Amazon EFS clients use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/using-amazon-efs-utils.html\"\u003eamazon-efs-utils package\u003c/a\u003e, an open source collection of tools, to connect securely to Amazon EFS file systems. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager\u003c/a\u003e gives you visibility and control of your infrastructure on AWS Cloud.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe integration of Amazon EFS with AWS Systems Manager is available in all AWS Regions. You can learn more by reading the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-efs-utils-with-aws-sys-manager.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, you can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e to easily create a file system in just two clicks and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager\"\u003eAWS Systems Manager console\u003c/a\u003e to manage your Amazon EFS clients.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-29T20:17:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-efs-integrates-aws-systems-manager-simplify-management-amazon-efs-clients/","postDateTime":"2020-09-29T10:29:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS integrates with AWS Systems Manager to simplify management of Amazon EFS clients","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) integrates with AWS Systems Manager to simplify management of Amazon EFS clients. You can now use AWS Systems Manager to automate the tasks required to install the latest version of the Amazon EFS client (amazon-efs-utils) package on your Amazon EC2 instances maintaining compliance and security by ensuring that the Amazon EFS client is kept up to date. Additionally, you can orchestrate file system mounts to multiple instances using a single command and improve visibility by monitoring the file system mount status using CloudWatch Logs. You do not need to login to your Amazon EC2 instances to manage your Amazon EFS clients.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-systems-manager","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-systems-manager","description":"general:products/aws-systems-manager","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-enforce-encryption-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-resources-using-aws-iam","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/enforce-encryption-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-resources-using-aws-iam/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:14:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/iam/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Identity and Access Management\u003c/a\u003e (AWS IAM) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_identity-vs-resource.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eidentity-based policies\u003c/a\u003e to enforce encryption of data at rest for your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) file system resources.  Using an IAM \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/list_amazonelasticfilesystem.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econdition key\u003c/a\u003e, you can prevent users from creating EFS file systems that aren’t encrypted.  Central security administrators can also define \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_type-auth.html#orgs_manage_policies_scp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eservice control policies\u003c/a\u003e (SCPs) inside \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/organizations/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Organizations\u003c/a\u003e to enforce EFS encryption for all AWS accounts in their organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability complements enforcing encryption of data in transit using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/create-file-system-policy.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003efile system policies\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/iam-access-control-nfs-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eIAM Authorization for NFS clients\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-for-amazon-efs-iam-authorization-and-access-points/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS Access Points\u003c/a\u003e as tools to manage access to your EFS resources at scale.  Enforcing encryption of data at rest is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions where EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e at no additional charge.  To get started, see the Amazon EFS user guide.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-16T21:41:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/enforce-encryption-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-resources-using-aws-iam/","postDateTime":"2020-09-16T11:16:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Enforce encryption for Amazon Elastic File System resources using AWS IAM","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/iam.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Identity and Access Management\u003c/a\u003e (AWS IAM) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_identity-vs-resource.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eidentity-based policies\u003c/a\u003e to enforce encryption of data at rest for your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) file system resources.  Using an IAM \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/list_amazonelasticfilesystem.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econdition key\u003c/a\u003e, you can prevent users from creating EFS file systems that aren’t encrypted.  Central security administrators can also define \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_type-auth.html#orgs_manage_policies_scp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eservice control policies\u003c/a\u003e (SCPs) inside \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/organizations.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Organizations\u003c/a\u003e to enforce EFS encryption for all AWS accounts in their organization.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-file-system","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-file-system","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-08-amazon-ek-on-aws-fargate-now-supports-amazon-efs-file-systems","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/08/amazon-ek-on-aws-fargate-now-supports-amazon-efs-file-systems/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) pods running on AWS Fargate can now mount Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems. AWS Fargate will use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-efs-csi-driver\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS CSI driver\u003c/a\u003e to automatically mount an EFS file system requested by a pod running on Fargate, without the need for manual driver installation. This enables persistent, regional, shared storage to be used by pods running on AWS Fargate, the serverless compute engine which allows customers to deploy and manage containerized applications without having to manage any of the underlying infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome examples of applications that can benefit from Kubernetes and elastic, durable shared storage are content management systems like WordPress and Drupal, developer tools like JIRA and Jenkins, machine learning frameworks like MXNet and Tensorflow, and data science tools like Jupyter and Airflow. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs of today, Fargate pods requiring EFS volumes can be started with newly created EKS clusters running Kubernetes version 1.17. Support for existing clusters will be rolled out over the coming weeks. To get started, follow the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEKS documentation\u003c/a\u003e to create a Kubernetes StorageClass and a PersistentVolumeClaim, then reference the PersistentVolumeClaim from the Fargate pods that require it. To learn more, you can visit the Amazon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/eks/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEKS product page\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/fargate/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Fargate product page\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-08-17T21:02:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/08/amazon-ek-on-aws-fargate-now-supports-amazon-efs-file-systems/","postDateTime":"2020-08-17T12:34:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EKS on AWS Fargate now supports Amazon EFS file systems","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) pods running on AWS Fargate can now mount Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems. AWS Fargate will use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-efs-csi-driver\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEFS CSI driver\u003c/a\u003e to automatically mount an EFS file system requested by a pod running on Fargate, without the need for manual driver installation. This enables persistent, regional, shared storage to be used by pods running on AWS Fargate, the serverless compute engine which allows customers to deploy and manage containerized applications without having to manage any of the underlying infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-file-system","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-file-system","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-fargate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-fargate","description":"general:products/aws-fargate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-efs-csi-driver-now-generally-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-efs-csi-driver-now-generally-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) CSI driver is now generally available. The EFS CSI driver makes it simple to configure elastic file storage for both EKS and self-managed Kubernetes clusters running on AWS using standard Kubernetes interfaces. Applications running in Kubernetes can use EFS file systems to share data between pods in a scale-out group, or with other applications running within or outside of Kubernetes. EFS can also help Kubernetes applications be highly available because all data written to EFS is written to multiple AWS Availability zones. If a Kubernetes pod is terminated and relaunched, the CSI driver will reconnect the EFS file system, even if the pod is relaunched in a different AWS Availability Zone.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the 1.0 release, the EFS CSI driver now has in-transit encryption enabled by default, helping companies meet their security and compliance goals. Additionally, the driver now supports EFS Access Points, application-specific entry points into an EFS file system that make it easier to share a file system between multiple pods. Access points can enforce a user identity for all file system requests that are made through the access point, and enforce a root directory for each pod.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome examples of applications that can benefit from Kubernetes and elastic, durable shared storage are content management systems like WordPress and Drupal, developer tools like JIRA and Jenkins, machine learning frameworks like MXNet and Tensorflow, and data science tools like Jupyter and Airflow. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, follow the getting started \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e to create a Kubernetes StorageClass and a PersistentVolumeClaim to provision, then reference the PersistentVolumeClaim from the pods that use it. To learn more, you can visit the Amazon EKS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/eks/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and the Amazon EFS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-24T17:54:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-efs-csi-driver-now-generally-available/","postDateTime":"2020-07-24T11:07:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS CSI Driver is now generally available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) CSI driver is now generally available. The EFS CSI driver makes it simple to configure elastic file storage for both EKS and self-managed Kubernetes clusters running on AWS using standard Kubernetes interfaces. Applications running in Kubernetes can use EFS file systems to share data between pods in a scale-out group, or with other applications running within or outside of Kubernetes. EFS can also help Kubernetes applications be highly available because all data written to EFS is written to multiple AWS Availability zones. If a Kubernetes pod is terminated and relaunched, the CSI driver will reconnect the EFS file system, even if the pod is relaunched in a different AWS Availability Zone.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-elastic-file-system-increases-per-client-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-elastic-file-system-increases-per-client-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports up to 500 MB/s of per-client throughput, a 100% increase from the previous limit of 250 MB/s. Total throughput for an EFS file system remains at 10+ GB/s across all NFS clients.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this launch, customers can benefit from increased performance and lower cost for workloads that require a high amount of throughput from a single or small number of instances. For example, file-based analytics workloads can now process more data in a shorter amount of time, reducing cost, backup applications can now store and retrieve backups faster, allowing for larger backups and reduced recovery times, and media encoding applications can achieve faster encoding times.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased per-client throughput is available today in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e, at no cost and with no action required. For more information, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Quotas and Limits\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-23T17:58:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-elastic-file-system-increases-per-client-throughput/","postDateTime":"2020-07-23T11:54:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System increases per-client throughput by 100%","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports up to 500 MB/s of per-client throughput, a 100% increase from the previous limit of 250 MB/s. Total throughput for an EFS file system remains at 10+ GB/s across all NFS clients.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-file-system","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-file-system","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-aws-announces-migration-acceleration-program-storage","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/aws-announces-migration-acceleration-program-storage/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:05:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS now offers the Migration Acceleration Program (MAP) for Storage. MAP for Storage provides services, best practices, and tools to help our\n customers save costs, accelerate their migrations, and modernize their \nstorage workloads on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMAP for Storage, an extension of the proven MAP methodology, assesses customer readiness along the dimensions of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/professional-services/CAF/\"\u003eAWS Cloud Adoption Framework\u003c/a\u003e. By leveraging the MAP for Storage methodology, we can help you build a migration plan, support the migration of your storage workloads on AWS, and provide you with incentives to help offset the costs associated with migrations. Workloads running on SAN or NAS systems that are well suited for storage  migration include on-premises data lakes, enterprise applications,  large unstructured data repositories, file shares, home directories,  backups, and archives, as well as containerized applications that need  to scale out.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAPN Partners and the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/professional-services/\"\u003eAWS Professional Services\u003c/a\u003e team help you execute migration plans and are experts in the MAP approach with proven experience managing large-scale migrations on AWS. With expert support, a proven methodology, and\u0026nbsp;over 14 years of experience running storage workloads for our customers, the MAP for Storage program will help simplify and accelerate your cloud migrations. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more on migrating your storage to AWS, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/products/storage/map-for-storage/\"\u003eMAP for Storage page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-08-27T21:22:49Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/aws-announces-migration-acceleration-program-storage/","postDateTime":"2020-07-08T10:58:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS announces the Migration Acceleration Program for Storage","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS now offers the Migration Acceleration Program (MAP) for Storage. MAP for Storage provides services, best practices, and tools to help our\n customers save costs, accelerate their migrations, and modernize their \nstorage workloads on AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-fsx-for-windows-file-server","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-fsx-for-windows-file-server","description":"general:products/amazon-fsx-for-windows-file-server","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:03+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-block-store","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-block-store","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-block-store","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-fsx-for-lustre","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-fsx-for-lustre","description":"general:products/amazon-fsx-for-lustre","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#customer-enablement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"customer-enablement","description":"marketing:marchitecture/customer-enablement","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"migration","description":"marketing:marchitecture/migration","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-industry#consulting-and-professional-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-industry","name":"consulting-and-professional-services","description":"marketing:industry/consulting-and-professional-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-amazon-efs-increases-file-system-minimum-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/amazon-efs--increases-file-system-minimum-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) file systems using the default bursting throughput mode now have a minimum throughput of 1 MiB/s. All EFS bursting mode file systems (regardless of size) can drive 100 MiB/s of throughput, and file systems with more than 1TiB of Standard class storage can drive 100 MiB/s per TB when burst credits are available. This change increases the minimum throughput from 50KiB/s per GiB of Standard class storage to a fixed minimum of 1 MiB/s for file systems with less than 20 GiB of Standard class storage, when burst credits are exhausted.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe recommend that you use AWS CloudWatch to monitor your burst credit balance. You can continue to configure Provisioned Throughput in situations where you need to instantly provision the throughput required for your applications independent of the amount of data stored in your file system. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll EFS file systems automatically have the new minimum throughput applied at no cost and with no action required. This change is available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall regions where EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about how EFS bursting mode file systems operate, see the Amazon EFS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-01T16:34:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/amazon-efs--increases-file-system-minimum-throughput/","postDateTime":"2020-06-30T10:05:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System increases file system minimum throughput","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) file systems using the default bursting throughput mode now have a minimum throughput of 1 MiB/s. All EFS bursting mode file systems (regardless of size) can drive 100 MiB/s of throughput, and file systems with more than 1TiB of Standard class storage can drive 100 MiB/s per TB when burst credits are available. This change increases the minimum throughput from 50KiB/s per GiB of Standard class storage to a fixed minimum of 1 MiB/s for file systems with less than 20 GiB of Standard class storage, when burst credits are exhausted.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-file-system","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-file-system","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-file-system","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:27+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-aws-datasync-can-now-transfer-data-to-from-aws-snowcone","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/aws-datasync-can-now-transfer-data-to-from-aws-snowcone/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:06:29+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e now supports transferring files to and from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/snowcone/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Snowcone\u003c/a\u003e, the smallest member of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/snow/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Snow Family\u003c/a\u003e of edge computing and data transfer devices. Snowcone is portable, ruggedized, and secure – small and light enough to fit in a backpack, and able to withstand harsh environments. The DataSync agent comes pre-installed on the device to transfer data online to and from Amazon S3, Amazon EFS, or Amazon FSx for Windows File Server.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can use Snowcone to deploy applications at the edge, and to collect, process, and move data to AWS. DataSync enables you to easily set up online transfers of files and objects between Snowcone and AWS Storage services. DataSync automates data transfers, including encryption, scheduling, monitoring, and data integrity validation. It is natively integrated with Amazon S3, Amazon EFS, Amazon FSx for Windows File Server, Amazon CloudWatch, and AWS CloudTrail, which provides seamless and secure access to your storage services, as well as detailed monitoring of the transfer.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSnowcone is available for customers in US locations, and can be used with DataSync to transfer to 22\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, view the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/snowcone/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSnowcone product page\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/introducing-aws-snowcone-small-lightweight-edge-storage-and-processing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSnowcone AWS News launch blog\u003c/a\u003e. To set up online data transfers, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/create-nfs-location.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDataSync documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and to get started, log in to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/importexport/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSnowcone console\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-23T21:13:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/aws-datasync-can-now-transfer-data-to-from-aws-snowcone/","postDateTime":"2020-06-17T12:28:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS DataSync can now transfer data to and from AWS Snowcone","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/datasync.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e now supports transferring files to and from \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/snowcone.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Snowcone\u003c/a\u003e, the smallest member of the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/snow.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Snow Family\u003c/a\u003e of edge computing and data transfer devices. Snowcone is portable, ruggedized, and secure – small and light enough to fit in a backpack, and able to withstand harsh environments. The DataSync agent comes pre-installed on the device to transfer data online to and from Amazon S3, Amazon EFS, or Amazon FSx for Windows File Server.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-snowcone","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-snowcone","description":"general:products/aws-snowcone","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:54+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-datasync","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-datasync","description":"general:products/aws-datasync","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-fsx-for-windows-file-server","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-fsx-for-windows-file-server","description":"general:products/amazon-fsx-for-windows-file-server","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:03+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"migration","description":"marketing:marchitecture/migration","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-aws-lambda-support-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-now-generally","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/aws-lambda-support-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-now-generally-/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Lambda customers can now enable functions to access Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). Customers can easily share data across function invocations, read large reference data files, and write function output to a persistent and shared data store.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now use AWS Lambda to build data-intensive applications, load larger libraries and models, process larger amounts of data in a highly distributed manner, and share data across functions, containers and instances. AWS Lambda will automatically mount the file system and provide a local path to read and write data at low latency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo use AWS Lambda with Amazon EFS, customers add an EFS Access Point ARN and the local mount path to their function configuration. AWS Lambda ensures function instances mount the EFS file system within the same Availability Zone in a few hundred milliseconds using TLS encryption. Customers setting up an EFS file system can enable encryption at rest, AWS IAM authorization, and choose the NFS permissions that Lambda functions use to access the file system via EFS Access Points.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Lambda support for Amazon EFS is available in all Regions where Lambda and EFS are available, with the exception of the Regions in China. For more information on availability, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region table\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, view our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-06-16T19:52:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/aws-lambda-support-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-now-generally-/","postDateTime":"2020-06-16T13:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Lambda support for Amazon Elastic File System now generally available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Lambda customers can now enable functions to access Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). Customers can easily share data across function invocations, read large reference data files, and write function output to a persistent and shared data store.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-lambda","description":"general:products/aws-lambda","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-use-case#big-data-analytics-and-business-intelligence-bi","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-use-case","name":"big-data-analytics-and-business-intelligence-(bi)","description":"general:use-case/big-data-analytics-and-business-intelligence-(bi)","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:58:10+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-use-case#web-and-web-apps","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-use-case","name":"web-and-web-apps","description":"general:use-case/web-and-web-apps","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:02:59+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-amazon-efs-now-available-milan","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-efs-now-available-milan/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:03:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the AWS Europe (Milan) region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-20T21:09:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-efs-now-available-milan/","postDateTime":"2020-05-20T10:26:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Europe (Milan) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the AWS Europe (Milan) region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-amazon-efs-now-available-cape-town","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-efs-now-available-cape-town/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:27:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the AWS Africa (Cape Town) region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-13T21:24:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-efs-now-available-cape-town/","postDateTime":"2020-05-13T09:59:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Africa (Cape Town) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers in the AWS Africa (Cape Town) region can now use Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-efs-updates-service-level-agreement-to-99-99-percent","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-efs-updates-service-level-agreement-to-99-99-percent/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has updated its \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/sla/\"\u003eservice level agreement (SLA) for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e to 99.99%.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously, Amazon EFS offered an SLA of 99.9%. Now, Amazon EFS has increased the SLA to 99.99%, improving our availability guarantee by a factor of 10.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe updated \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/sla/\"\u003eSLA\u003c/a\u003e is available immediately in all regions where EFS is available. For more information on where Amazon EFS is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon EFS. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-30T19:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-efs-updates-service-level-agreement-to-99-99-percent/","postDateTime":"2020-04-30T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Updates Service Level Agreement to 99.99%","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has updated its \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs/sla.html\"\u003eservice level agreement (SLA) for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e to 99.99%.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-aws-datasync-enhances-monitoring-capabilities-with-file-level-logging","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/aws-datasync-enhances-monitoring-capabilities-with-file-level-logging/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWhen using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;you can now enable detailed logging for files and objects copied between your NFS servers, SMB servers, Amazon S3 buckets, Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems, and Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file systems. Logging of individual files enables you to identify what was transferred at a given time, as well as the results of the content integrity verification performed by DataSync. This simplifies monitoring, reporting, and troubleshooting, and enables you to provide timely updates to stakeholders.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen creating or editing a DataSync task, you can specify an Amazon CloudWatch log group, and choose detailed logging. DataSync will log the name, size, and timestamp for each transferred file or object. A second log entry will be published for each file or object when its content is verified against the source storage. The combination of these new CloudWatch Logs, alongside the existing CloudWatch graphs embedded in the DataSync console, and CloudWatch metrics published by DataSync, provides you with end-to-end monitoring of your data transfers, including throughput and file-level transfer status. DataSync also publishes CloudWatch events that you can use to trigger notifications or automate post-processing at the end of your task.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis new logging option is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregions where AWS DataSync is available\u003c/a\u003e. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eCharges for CloudWatch Logs\u003c/a\u003e apply when you enable logging. You can learn more in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/creating-task.html#configuring-task\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDataSync documentation\u003c/a\u003e, or log in to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync console\u003c/a\u003e to get started. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-23T21:13:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/aws-datasync-enhances-monitoring-capabilities-with-file-level-logging/","postDateTime":"2020-04-24T09:18:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS DataSync enhances monitoring capabilities with file-level logging","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWhen using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/datasync.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;you can now enable detailed logging for files and objects copied between your NFS servers, SMB servers, Amazon S3 buckets, Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems, and Amazon FSx for Windows File Server file systems. Logging of individual files enables you to identify what was transferred at a given time, as well as the results of the content integrity verification performed by DataSync. This simplifies monitoring, reporting, and troubleshooting, and enables you to provide timely updates to stakeholders.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"migration","description":"marketing:marchitecture/migration","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-datasync","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-datasync","description":"general:products/aws-datasync","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-ecs-aws-fargate-support-amazon-efs-filesystems-generally-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-ecs-aws-fargate-support-amazon-efs-filesystems-generally-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) tasks running on both Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) and AWS Fargate can now mount Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems. ECS tasks using EFS will automatically mount the file systems specified by the customer in the task definition and make them available to the containers in the task across all availability zones in the region. This enables persistent, shared storage to be defined and used at the task and container level in ECS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApplications like Wordpress, Drupal, and JIRA use EFS to store user data and application state, with active/standby container pairs running in different availability zones for high availability. Data science teams use EFS to store shared training data and home directories, allowing notebook containers and distributed training jobs to access the data in parallel.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo use EFS with ECS, customers can add one or more volume definitions to an ECS task definition.  A volume definition includes an EFS file system ID, Access Point ID, and whether to enable IAM authorization or TLS encryption in transit.  Container definitions within the task definition can specify the task definition volumes that should be mounted when that container is run.  When a task that uses an EFS filesystem runs, ECS ensures that the EFS file system is mounted and available to the containers that need access to it. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon ECS support for EFS is available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall regions where ECS and EFS are available\u003c/a\u003e. To get started, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/APIReference/API_EFSVolumeConfiguration.html\"\u003eview our documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-17T16:07:54Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-ecs-aws-fargate-support-amazon-efs-filesystems-generally-available/","postDateTime":"2020-04-08T15:44:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon ECS and AWS Fargate support for Amazon EFS File Systems now generally available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic Container Service (ECS) tasks running on both Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) and AWS Fargate can now mount Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems. ECS tasks using EFS will automatically mount the file systems specified by the customer in the task definition and make them available to the containers in the task across all availability zones in the region. This enables persistent, shared storage to be defined and used at the task and container level in ECS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-fargate","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-fargate","description":"general:products/aws-fargate","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ecs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ecs","description":"general:products/amazon-ecs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#containers-and-deployment","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"containers-and-deployment","description":"marketing:marchitecture/containers-and-deployment","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-elastic-file-system-announces-increase-in-read-operations-for-general-purpose-file-systems","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-elastic-file-system-announces-increase-in-read-operations-for-general-purpose-file-systems/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:01:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS)\u0026nbsp;General Purpose mode file systems support up to 35,000 read operations per second, a 400% increase from the previous limit of 7,000. Maximum write operations are unchanged at 7,000 per second.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGeneral Purpose mode (GP mode) is the default performance mode for Amazon EFS. It offers the lowest per-operation latency and is the recommended choice for most applications. Amazon EFS also offers the Max I/O performance mode which can scale to higher levels of aggregate throughput and supports over 500,000 operations per second with slightly higher metadata latencies than GP mode.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this launch, customers benefit from increased performance for workloads that need the lower metadata latencies of GP mode but also require a higher number of read operations. For example, customers using Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) software can now host more application instances on a single file system, lowering cost and reducing operational complexity, while customers with CI/CD workloads can enjoy faster software builds, increasing developer productivity. Other use cases that benefit include web serving, document management, and Electronic Document Interchange (EDI).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll existing and new GP file systems automatically have the new read operations limit enabled at no additional cost and with no action required. The new limit is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregions where EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e. For additional details on how read and write operations contribute to total file operations,\u0026nbsp;see the Amazon EFS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/limits.html#limits-fs-specific\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-01T14:45:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-elastic-file-system-announces-increase-in-read-operations-for-general-purpose-file-systems/","postDateTime":"2020-04-01T11:31:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System announces 400% increase in read operations for General Purpose mode file systems","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS)\u0026nbsp;General Purpose mode file systems support up to 35,000 read operations per second, a 400% increase from the previous limit of 7,000. Maximum write operations are unchanged at 7,000 per second.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-02-aws-codebuild-adds-support-for-amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/aws-codebuild-adds-support-for-amazon-efs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T12:59:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Filesystem\u003c/a\u003e (EFS) in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/codebuild/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CodeBuild\u003c/a\u003e build jobs. This can be achieved by specifying the EFS file system Id in your CodeBuild \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/working-with-build-projects.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProject\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can specify one or more EFS filesystem Id as part of their CodeBuild Project. When a build that uses an EFS filesystem is triggered, CodeBuild ensures that the EFS filesystem is mounted and available to access for any commands specified in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html#build-spec-ref-syntax\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ebuildspec\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS CodeBuild\u0027s support for EFS is available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where CodeBuild and EFS are available\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/codebuild/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e or the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about how to get started with AWS CodeBuild.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-02-06T20:32:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/aws-codebuild-adds-support-for-amazon-efs/","postDateTime":"2020-02-06T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS CodeBuild Adds Support for Amazon EFS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Filesystem\u003c/a\u003e (EFS) in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/codebuild.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CodeBuild\u003c/a\u003e build jobs. This can be achieved by specifying the EFS file system Id in your CodeBuild \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/working-with-build-projects.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eProject\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#developer-tools","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"developer-tools","description":"marketing:marchitecture/developer-tools","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:40:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:40:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-codebuild","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-codebuild","description":"general:products/aws-codebuild","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-02-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:03:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US-East) Region\u003c/a\u003e. With this launch, Amazon EFS is now available in all standard AWS Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-02-05T21:07:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/02/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-east-region/","postDateTime":"2020-02-05T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US-East) Region\u003c/a\u003e. With this launch, Amazon EFS is now available in all standard AWS Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-amazon-efs-available-in-aws-china","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-efs-available-in-aws-china/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:00:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD and the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed, and elastic NFS  file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources.  It is built to scale on demand without disrupting applications, to grow  and shrink automatically with files, and to eliminate the need to manage  capacity. Amazon EFS is a regional service storing data within and  across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) for high availability and  durability. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.amazonaws.cn/en/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-22T21:16:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-efs-available-in-aws-china/","postDateTime":"2020-01-22T11:25:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD and the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-aws-backup-delivers-fast-restore-experience-amazon-efs-item-level-recovery","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/aws-backup-delivers-fast-restore-experience-amazon-efs-item-level-recovery/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:04:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup now provides a streamlined experience for Amazon Elastic File  System (EFS) Item-Level Recovery. You can now use AWS Backup to perform  granular recovery of individual files or folders from Amazon EFS  backups using a centralized console, for a simplified and fast restore  experience, to meet more stringent Recovery Time Objective (RTO)  requirements. To get started, choose the “Item-level Restore” restore  type and provide one or more paths you want to recover using the AWS  Backup console, SDK or CLI. This release is a continuation of our  commitment to make data protection as streamlined and scalable as  possible for our customers.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor step-by-step guidance on how to recover individual files or directories, please see the AWS Backup documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/?id\u003ddocs_gateway\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup offers a centralized, fully-managed, policy-based service to back up data across AWS services. With AWS Backup, you can centrally configure backup scheduling, set retention policies and monitor backup activity for different AWS resources, including Amazon Elastic Cloud Compute (EC2) instances, Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) volumes, Amazon Relational Database Service (RDS) databases, Amazon DynamoDB tables, Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) file systems, and AWS Storage Gateway volumes.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all regions where AWS Backup is available for Amazon EFS. To learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product pages and documentation.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-14T00:23:01Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/aws-backup-delivers-fast-restore-experience-amazon-efs-item-level-recovery/","postDateTime":"2020-01-13T11:05:53Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Backup Delivers Fast Restore Experience for Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) Item-Level Recovery","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup now provides a streamlined experience for Amazon Elastic File  System (EFS) Item-Level Recovery. You can now use AWS Backup to perform  granular recovery of individual files or folders from Amazon EFS  backups using a centralized console, for a simplified and fast restore  experience, to meet more stringent Recovery Time Objective (RTO)  requirements. To get started, choose the “Item-level Restore” restore  type and provide one or more paths you want to recover using the AWS  Backup console, SDK or CLI. This release is a continuation of our  commitment to make data protection as streamlined and scalable as  possible for our customers.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-backup","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-backup","description":"general:products/aws-backup","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-amazon-elastic-file-system-introduces-efs-access-points","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-introduces-efs-access-points/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:02:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Access Points is a new EFS feature that simplifies providing applications access to shared data sets in an EFS file system. EFS Access Points work together with AWS IAM and enforce an operating system user and group, and a directory for every file system request made through the access point. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS Access Points represent a new way to manage application access in NFS environments with increased scalability, security, and ease of use. Use cases that can benefit from EFS Access Points include container-based environments where developers build and deploy their own containers, data science applications that require access to production data, and sharing a specific directory in your file system with other AWS accounts.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing access points is easy. With a few clicks in the EFS console, you can create an access point for your file system with an identity and a directory customized for your application. You can also update your file system’s IAM policy to refer to access points, for example, to require a specific IAM identity for a given access point. To use an access point, download the updated EFS mount helper from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/efs-utils\"\u003eGithub\u003c/a\u003e and mount your file system with the ‘-o accesspoint\u003d’ mount option.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS Access Points is available today in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall regions where Amazon EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e, at no additional charge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-for-amazon-efs-iam-authorization-and-access-points\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-access-points.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or log in to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e to get started. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-14T17:21:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-introduces-efs-access-points/","postDateTime":"2020-01-13T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System introduces EFS Access Points","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Access Points is a new EFS feature that simplifies providing applications access to shared data sets in an EFS file system. EFS Access Points work together with AWS IAM and enforce an operating system user and group, and a directory for every file system request made through the access point. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-now-supports-aws-identity-and-access-management-iam-for-network-file-system-clients","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-now-supports-aws-identity-and-access-management-iam-for-network-file-system-clients/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:01:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) to manage Network File System (NFS) access for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). You can use IAM roles to identify NFS clients with cryptographic security and use IAM policies to manage client-specific permissions. This new capability provides a simplified way to manage access at scale in NFS environments and is complementary to network-based security controls. With IAM for NFS clients you can use the same tools and processes you use today for managing access to other AWS resources. Permission checks are logged to AWS CloudTrail so you can audit client access to your file system.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing IAM for NFS clients is easy. With just a few clicks in the EFS console, you can apply common policies to your file system such as disabling root access, enforcing read-only access, or enforcing that all connections to your file system are encrypted. You can also apply more advanced policies such as granting access to specific IAM roles, including those in other AWS accounts. To use policies that grant access to specific IAM roles, enable your NFS clients to share their IAM identity with EFS by downloading the updated mount helper from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/efs-utils\"\u003eGithub\u003c/a\u003e and mounting your file system with the ‘-o iam’ mount option.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIAM for NFS clients is available today in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall regions where Amazon EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e, at no additional charge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, please read the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-for-amazon-efs-iam-authorization-and-access-points\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/auth-and-access-control.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or log in to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e to get started.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-14T17:19:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-now-supports-aws-identity-and-access-management-iam-for-network-file-system-clients/","postDateTime":"2020-01-13T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System now supports AWS Identity and Access Management for Network File System clients","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) to manage Network File System (NFS) access for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). You can use IAM roles to identify NFS clients with cryptographic security and use IAM policies to manage client-specific permissions. This new capability provides a simplified way to manage access at scale in NFS environments and is complementary to network-based security controls. With IAM for NFS clients you can use the same tools and processes you use today for managing access to other AWS resources. Permission checks are logged to AWS CloudTrail so you can audit client access to your file system.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-elastic-file-system-now-supports-service-linked-roles","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-elastic-file-system-now-supports-service-linked-roles/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:26:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is introducing support for using AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_terms-and-concepts.html#iam-term-service-linked-role\"\u003eservice-linked roles\u003c/a\u003e, a type of IAM role that allows you to easily delegate permissions to AWS services and gain additional transparency into when they are used on your behalf.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe EFS service-linked role is predefined by Amazon EFS and includes permissions that the service requires to use other AWS services on your behalf. Examples include creating and deleting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic Compute Cloud\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EC2) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-eni.html\"\u003eElastic Network Interfaces\u003c/a\u003e (ENIs) that Amazon EFS uses for the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/accessing-fs.html\"\u003emount targets\u003c/a\u003e you use to access your EFS file systems.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnlike a normal IAM role, you cannot delete the service-linked role if it is still in use by an Amazon EFS file system. This protects you from inadvertently revoking Amazon EFS\u0027s required permissions to your resources. The addition of a service-linked role to Amazon EFS also helps with monitoring and auditing requirements in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/logging-using-cloudtrail.html\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e by logging actions performed by Amazon EFS against its service-linked role.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon EFS service-linked role is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon EFS is available, at no additional charge. To learn more about Amazon EFS and its service linked role, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/using-service-linked-roles.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS user guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-19T21:23:17Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-elastic-file-system-now-supports-service-linked-roles/","postDateTime":"2019-12-19T11:39:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System Now Supports Service-Linked Roles","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is introducing support for using AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_terms-and-concepts.html#iam-term-service-linked-role\"\u003eservice-linked roles\u003c/a\u003e, a type of IAM role that allows you to easily delegate permissions to AWS services and gain additional transparency into when they are used on your behalf.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-elastic-files-system-now-available-in-bahrain-stockholm-sau-paulo-hong-kong","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-elastic-files-system-now-available-in-bahrain-stockholm-sau-paulo-hong-kong/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in all commercial AWS regions except China regions.  With this launch, Amazon EFS is now also available in the regions below:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAsia Pacific (Hong Kong)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEurope (Stockholm)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMiddle East (Bahrain)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSouth America (São Paulo) \u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-20T18:48:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-elastic-files-system-now-available-in-bahrain-stockholm-sau-paulo-hong-kong/","postDateTime":"2019-11-20T12:48:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in Middle East (Bahrain), Europe (Stockholm), South America (São Paulo) and Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in all commercial AWS regions except China regions.  With this launch, Amazon EFS is now also available in the regions below:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAsia Pacific (Hong Kong)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEurope (Stockholm)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMiddle East (Bahrain)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSouth America (São Paulo) \u0026nbsp;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-elastic-file-system-infrequent-access-now-supports-7-day-lifecycle-management-policy","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-elastic-file-system-infrequent-access-now-supports-7-day-lifecycle-management-policy/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:19:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now choose an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Lifecycle Management policy to automatically move files that haven’t been accessed for 7 days into the EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) storage class and save up to 92% as your access patterns change.  You can configure this new policy option for your file system, or you can use one of the existing policy options: 14, 30, 60, or 90 days.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS IA provides price/performance that’s cost-optimized for files not accessed every day, enabling you to save up to 92% on file storage costs compared to the Amazon EFS Standard storage class. To get started with EFS IA, you enable Lifecycle Management for your file system, which automatically moves files to the lower-cost storage class based on the last time they were accessed.  With this launch, EFS customers can now more quickly realize cost savings and further reduce their first month’s storage charges for workloads where files become infrequently accessed 1 week after they’re initially loaded. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis new option for EFS Lifecycle Management is immediately available in all EFS regions. For EFS regional availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/features/infrequent-access/\"\u003eEFS IA and EFS Lifecycle Management\u003c/a\u003e, try it out in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAWS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-06T18:08:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-elastic-file-system-infrequent-access-now-supports-7-day-lifecycle-management-policy/","postDateTime":"2019-11-06T11:48:15Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System Infrequent Access Now Supports a 7-day Lifecycle Management Policy","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now choose an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Lifecycle Management policy to automatically move files that haven’t been accessed for 7 days into the EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) storage class and save up to 92% as your access patterns change.  You can configure this new policy option for your file system, or you can use one of the existing policy options: 14, 30, 60, or 90 days.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-efs-supports-aws-privatelink","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-efs-supports-aws-privatelink/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e to create Amazon VPC interface endpoints for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e. AWS PrivateLink provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and on-premises applications, securely on the Amazon network. Amazon EFS customers can now use private IP connectivity and security groups to meet their specific compliance requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic NFS file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Amazon EFS already supports industry standard TLS to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-in-transit/\"\u003esecure encryption of data in transit\u003c/a\u003e, and all clients connect to Amazon EFS from within their Virtual Private Cloud (VPC). With today’s launch, you can improve your compliance posture by using AWS PrivateLink to automate the creation and management of your Amazon EFS file systems using the EFS API, without using public IP addresses and without any traffic traversing the internet.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo use AWS PrivateLink, create an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpce-interface.html\"\u003einterface VPC endpoint\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon EFS in your VPC using the Amazon VPC console, SDK or CLI. You can also access the VPC endpoint from on-premises environments or from other VPCs using AWS VPN, AWS Direct Connect, or VPC Peering.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available in all regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rande.html#elasticfilesystem-region\"\u003eAmazon EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS website\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;read the EFS VPC endpoint \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-vpc-endpoints.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, or get started in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/vpc/home\"\u003eAWS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2021-10-11T18:30:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-efs-supports-aws-privatelink/","postDateTime":"2019-10-22T09:10:56Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now supports AWS PrivateLink","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/privatelink.html\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e to create Amazon VPC interface endpoints for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e. AWS PrivateLink provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and on-premises applications, securely on the Amazon network. Amazon EFS customers can now use private IP connectivity and security groups to meet their specific compliance requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#security-identity-and-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"security-identity-and-compliance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/security-identity-and-compliance","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-efs-now-in-ec2-launch-instance-wizard","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-efs-now-in-ec2-launch-instance-wizard/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:18:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:36:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure Amazon EC2 instances to mount \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;file systems using the EC2 Launch Instance Wizard. This integration simplifies the process of configuring EC2 instances to mount EFS file systems at launch time with recommended mount options. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Multiple EC2 instances can mount an EFS file system and share file data using standard Linux tools and commands. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS file systems are often used for web serving and content management, application development and testing, media and entertainment workflows, machine learning and data science notebooks, database backups, container storage, and enterprise applications that utilize shared storage.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, open the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/ec2/v2/home?#LaunchInstanceWizard:\"\u003eEC2 Launch Instance Wizard\u003c/a\u003e and select the EFS file system you want to mount from \u003cb\u003eStep 3: Configure Instance Details\u003c/b\u003e, or click \u003cb\u003eCreate new file system\u003c/b\u003e. To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/launching-instance.html\"\u003eEC2 Launch Instance Wizard documentation\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/whatisefs.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-17T17:40:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-efs-now-in-ec2-launch-instance-wizard/","postDateTime":"2019-10-17T15:22:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now in the EC2 Launch Instance Wizard","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure Amazon EC2 instances to mount \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;file systems using the EC2 Launch Instance Wizard. This integration simplifies the process of configuring EC2 instances to mount EFS file systems at launch time with recommended mount options. Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Multiple EC2 instances can mount an EFS file system and share file data using standard Linux tools and commands. \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-09-amazon-eks-announces-beta-release-of-amazon-efs-csi-driver","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/amazon-eks-announces-beta-release-of-amazon-efs-csi-driver/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:39:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) CSI driver is now supported by Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS). The EFS CSI driver makes it simple to configure elastic file storage for both EKS and self-managed Kubernetes clusters running on AWS using standard Kubernetes interfaces. Applications running in Kubernetes can use EFS file systems to share data between pods in a scale-out group, or with other applications running within or outside of Kubernetes. EFS can also help Kubernetes applications be highly available because all data written to EFS is written to multiple AWS Availability zones. If a Kubernetes pod is terminated and relaunched, the CSI driver will reconnect the EFS file system, even if the pod is relaunched in a different AWS Availability Zone.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome examples of applications that can benefit from Kubernetes and elastic, durable shared storage are content management systems like WordPress and Drupal, developer tools like JIRA and Artifactory, machine learning frameworks like MXNet and Tensorflow, and data science notebooks like Jupyter and Jupyterhub.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, follow the getting started \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e to create a Kubernetes StorageClass and a PersistentVolumeClaim to provision, then reference the PersistentVolumeClaim from the pods that use it. To learn more, you can visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/eks/\"\u003eAmazon EKS product page\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:38Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/amazon-eks-announces-beta-release-of-amazon-efs-csi-driver/","postDateTime":"2019-09-19T11:49:31Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EKS Announces Support for the Amazon EFS CSI Driver","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) CSI driver is now supported by Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS). The EFS CSI driver makes it simple to configure elastic file storage for both EKS and self-managed Kubernetes clusters running on AWS using standard Kubernetes interfaces. Applications running in Kubernetes can use EFS file systems to share data between pods in a scale-out group, or with other applications running within or outside of Kubernetes. EFS can also help Kubernetes applications be highly available because all data written to EFS is written to multiple AWS Availability zones. If a Kubernetes pod is terminated and relaunched, the CSI driver will reconnect the EFS file system, even if the pod is relaunched in a different AWS Availability Zone.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"compute","description":"marketing:marchitecture/compute","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eks","description":"general:products/amazon-eks","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-09-manage-your-amazon-efs-limits-with-aws-service-quotas","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/manage-your-amazon-efs-limits-with-aws-service-quotas/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:18:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now view and manage your limits for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) using AWS Service Quotas.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, fully managed elastic NFS file system for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, eliminating the need to provision and manage capacity to accommodate growth.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith AWS Service Quotas, you can view and manage your quotas easily and at scale as your AWS workloads grow. Quotas, also referred to as limits, are the maximum number of resources that you can create in an AWS account.  You can now view your EFS limits and request increases for your account-level EFS limits using Service Quotas via the AWS console, AWS APIs and the AWS CLI. AWS Service Quotas is available at no additional charge. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can view and manage your Amazon EFS limits through AWS Service Quotas in all commercial AWS regions where EFS is available. For Amazon EFS regional availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. Explore \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://console.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/\"\u003eService Quotas\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS console. To learn more about Service Quotas, review the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/mt/introducing-service-quotas-view-and-manage-your-quotas-for-aws-services-from-one-central-location/\"\u003eService Quotas Blog\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/manage-your-amazon-efs-limits-with-aws-service-quotas/","postDateTime":"2019-09-10T14:36:23Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Manage your Amazon EFS limits with AWS Service Quotas","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now view and manage your limits for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) using AWS Service Quotas.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-09-announcing-amazon-efs-price-reduction-for-infrequent-access-storage","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/announcing-amazon-efs-price-reduction-for-infrequent-access-storage/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:15:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now save even more money on your file storage - automatically - as your access patterns change when using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/features/infrequent-access/\"\u003eInfrequent Access storage class\u003c/a\u003e (EFS IA). Today we’re announcing a 44% reduction* in storage prices for EFS IA, one of the largest percentage price reductions in AWS history to date. EFS IA storage prices now start at $0.025/GB-month. Using the industry accepted estimate that 20% of data is actively used and 80% is infrequently accessed, this reduction leads to an effective EFS storage price of $0.08/GB-month (20% * $0.30/GB-month for files stored on EFS Standard + 80% * $0.025/GB-month for files stored on EFS IA \u003d $0.08/GB-month)*.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll Amazon EFS file systems transparently serve data from two storage classes - EFS Standard and EFS IA - so you don’t have to worry about which of your files are actively used and which are infrequently accessed. EFS IA provides price/performance that’s cost-optimized for files not accessed every day, with storage prices up to 92% lower compared to EFS Standard. To load data into EFS IA, simply enable EFS Lifecycle Management, a capability that monitors your access patterns and moves files across the two EFS storage classes according to the policy you choose.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis price reduction is available in all EFS regions effective as of September 1st, 2019.  For more information about EFS regional availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.  For EFS IA pricing, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\"\u003eEFS Pricing page\u003c/a\u003e.  To get started with EFS Infrequent Access and Lifecycle Management, try it out in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAmazon EFS console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can read more about EFS IA and its updated pricing in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/optimize-storage-cost-with-reduced-pricing-for-amazon-efs-infrequent-access/\"\u003eAWS News Blog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003e*Pricing in the US East (N. Virginia) region.\u003c/i\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/09/announcing-amazon-efs-price-reduction-for-infrequent-access-storage/","postDateTime":"2019-09-04T11:06:11Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing Amazon EFS price reduction for Infrequent Access storage","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now save even more money on your file storage - automatically - as your access patterns change when using the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs/features/infrequent-access.html\"\u003eInfrequent Access storage class\u003c/a\u003e (EFS IA). Today we’re announcing a 44% reduction* in storage prices for EFS IA, one of the largest percentage price reductions in AWS history to date. EFS IA storage prices now start at $0.025/GB-month. Using the industry accepted estimate that 20% of data is actively used and 80% is infrequently accessed, this reduction leads to an effective EFS storage price of $0.08/GB-month (20% * $0.30/GB-month for files stored on EFS Standard + 80% * $0.025/GB-month for files stored on EFS IA \u003d $0.08/GB-month)*.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-08-amazon-sagemaker-works-with-amazon-fsx-lustre-amazon-efs-model-training","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-sagemaker-works-with-amazon-fsx-lustre-amazon-efs-model-training/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:20:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/\"\u003eAmazon SageMaker\u003c/a\u003e now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/fsx/lustre/\"\u003eAmazon FSx for Lustre\u003c/a\u003e file systems as data sources for training machine learning models on SageMaker. Amazon FSx for Lustre is a high performance file system optimized for workloads, such as machine learning, analytics and high performance computing. Amazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Support for these file systems accelerates and simplifies using Amazon SageMaker to train models with data sets. The file system data source reduces the start-up time by eliminating the data download step of the training process and leveraging the various performance and throughput benefits of the file system to execute the training job faster.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUntil today, Amazon SageMaker transparently downloaded a full training set from Amazon S3 to local file storage at the start of a training job, when using the File input mode. Now with Amazon FSx for Lustre, customers can accelerate their File mode training jobs by avoiding the initial Amazon S3 download time. When Amazon FSx for Lustre file system is linked to Amazon S3 buckets, it automatically copies objects from Amazon S3 to the file system when objects are accessed for the first time. The same FSx file system can also be used across multiple SageMaker jobs, preventing repeated downloading of common objects. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso until today, customers could only use Amazon SageMaker with training sets stored on Amazon S3. Now, customers can also use training sets that are stored on Amazon EFS. Amazon SageMaker interacts directly with Amazon EFS, eliminating the need to copy data sets from Amazon EFS to Amazon S3 for use with Amazon SageMaker. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMost Amazon SageMaker built-in machine learning algorithms support EFS and FSx for Lustre as input data source. This feature is available in all regions where the respective file systems are available. For details on region availability please check the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/latest/dg/API_CreateTrainingJob.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e for more information and read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/speed-up-training-on-amazon-sagemaker-using-amazon-efs-or-amazon-fsx-for-lustre-file-systems/\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e for how to use the feature.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:13Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-sagemaker-works-with-amazon-fsx-lustre-amazon-efs-model-training/","postDateTime":"2019-08-27T08:26:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon SageMaker Now Works With Amazon FSx For Lustre and Amazon EFS, Accelerating And Simplifying Model Training","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/sagemaker.html\"\u003eAmazon SageMaker\u003c/a\u003e now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) and \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/fsx/lustre.html\"\u003eAmazon FSx for Lustre\u003c/a\u003e file systems as data sources for training machine learning models on SageMaker. Amazon FSx for Lustre is a high performance file system optimized for workloads, such as machine learning, analytics and high performance computing. Amazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Support for these file systems accelerates and simplifies using Amazon SageMaker to train models with data sets. The file system data source reduces the start-up time by eliminating the data download step of the training process and leveraging the various performance and throughput benefits of the file system to execute the training job faster.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-sagemaker","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-sagemaker","description":"general:products/amazon-sagemaker","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:39+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-machine-learning","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-machine-learning","description":"general:products/amazon-machine-learning","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T17:58:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-fsx-for-lustre","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-fsx-for-lustre","description":"general:products/amazon-fsx-for-lustre","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-07-configuration-update-for-amazon-efs-encryption-data-in-transit","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/configuration-update-for-amazon-efs-encryption-data-in-transit/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe’ve updated the default configuration for the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e mount helper package when using encryption of data in transit.  Starting today, use of the Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) is not enabled by default.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon EFS mount helper provides the option to encrypt data in transit for EFS file systems using Transport Layer Security version 1.2 (TLS v1.2). EFS uses an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.amazontrust.com/\"\u003eAmazon certificate authority\u003c/a\u003e (CA) to issue and sign its TLS certificates, as well as to check for certificate revocation using OCSP. The OCSP endpoint must be accessible over the Internet from your Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) in order to check for certificate revocation. To maximize file system availability in the event that the CA is not reachable from your VPC, the EFS mount helper no longer enables OCSP by default. Within the service, EFS continuously monitors for certificate revocation status and will issue new certificates if a revoked certificate is detected.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can still choose to enable OCSP to have your clients check for revoked certificates, providing the strongest possible security. OCSP protects against malicious use of revoked certificates, which is unlikely to occur within your VPC. In the event that an EFS TLS certificate is revoked, Amazon will publish a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/security/security-bulletins/\"\u003esecurity bulletin\u003c/a\u003e and make a new version of the EFS mount helper available that explicitly rejects the revoked certificate.\u0026nbsp; This will require you to update the EFS mount helper manually.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe updated EFS mount helper is available within \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/amazon-linux-ami/\"\u003eAmazon Linux\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/amazon-linux-2/\"\u003eAmazon Linux 2\u003c/a\u003e AMIs, and can also be found on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/efs-utils\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e.  To get started with the Amazon EFS mount helper and EFS encryption of data in transit, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/encryption.html#encryption-in-transit\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/amazon-linux-2/\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/configuration-update-for-amazon-efs-encryption-data-in-transit/","postDateTime":"2019-07-23T12:37:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Configuration update for Amazon EFS encryption of data in transit","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe’ve updated the default configuration for the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e mount helper package when using encryption of data in transit.  Starting today, use of the Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) is not enabled by default.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-07-optimize-cost-amazon-efs-infrequent-access-lifecycle-management","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/optimize-cost-amazon-efs-infrequent-access-lifecycle-management/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:31+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now choose from four Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Lifecycle Management policies to automatically move files into the EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) storage class and save up to 85% as your access patterns change.  Additionally, you can now enable Lifecycle Management for all EFS file systems.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS IA provides price/performance that’s cost-optimized for files not accessed every day, enabling you to save up to 85% on file storage costs compared to the Amazon EFS Standard storage class. To get started with EFS IA, you enable Lifecycle Management for your file system, which automatically moves files to the lower-cost storage class based on the last time they were accessed. You can now choose age-off policies of 14, 30, 60, or 90 days. Previously, EFS Lifecycle Management used a pre-defined policy to move files into EFS IA.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese enhancements are immediately available in all EFS regions.  For EFS regional availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.  To get started with EFS IA and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/features/infrequent-access/\"\u003eEFS Lifecycle Management\u003c/a\u003e, try it out in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs\"\u003eAWS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/optimize-cost-amazon-efs-infrequent-access-lifecycle-management/","postDateTime":"2019-07-09T13:11:39Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Optimize Cost with Amazon EFS Infrequent Access Lifecycle Management ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now choose from four Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Lifecycle Management policies to automatically move files into the EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) storage class and save up to 85% as your access patterns change.  Additionally, you can now enable Lifecycle Management for all EFS file systems.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-backup-amazon-efs-file-systems-us-west-canada-europe-asia-pacific","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/backup-amazon-efs-file-systems-us-west-canada-europe-asia-pacific/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:39+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e, an automated and centralized backup service, to backup Amazon EFS file systems in the AWS US West (N. California), Canada (Central), Europe (London), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Seoul) Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is a fully managed backup service that makes it easy to centralize and automate the back up of data across AWS services in the cloud as well as on premises. With AWS Backup, protecting your AWS resources, such as Amazon EFS file systems, is as easy as a few clicks in the AWS Backup console. Customers can configure and audit the AWS resources they want to back up, automate backup scheduling, set retention policies, and monitor all recent backup and restore activity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS integration with AWS Backup removes the need for costly, customer solutions or manual processes by providing a fully managed, policy based backup solution that provides automated backup scheduling and backup retention management.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is available in the US East (Northern Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon), Canada (Central), Europe (London), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Seoul) regions. For more information on where Amazon EFS and AWS Backup is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. For pricing information in your region, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/pricing/\"\u003eAWS Backup pricing page\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about Amazon EFS integration with AWS Backup, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\"\u003eAWS Backup product page\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html\"\u003eAWS Backup documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/backup-amazon-efs-file-systems-us-west-canada-europe-asia-pacific/","postDateTime":"2019-06-27T10:29:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Back up Amazon EFS file systems in US West (N. California), Canada (Central), Europe (London), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Seoul) with AWS Backup","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/backup.html\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e, an automated and centralized backup service, to backup Amazon EFS file systems in the AWS US West (N. California), Canada (Central), Europe (London), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Seoul) Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-europe-paris-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-europe-paris-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Europe (Paris) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need – when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies. Amazon EFS is a fully managed service that requires no changes to your existing applications and tools, providing access through a standard file system interface for seamless integration. There is a Standard and an Infrequent Access storage class available with Amazon EFS. Using Lifecycle Management, files not accessed for 30 days will automatically be moved to a cost-optimized Infrequent Access storage class, giving you a simple way to store and access active and infrequently accessed file system data in the same file system while reducing storage costs by up to 85%. Amazon EFS is a regional service storing data within and across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) for high availability and durability. You can access your file systems across AZs, regions, and VPCs and share files between thousands of Amazon EC2 instances and on-premises servers via AWS Direct Connect or AWS VPN.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases from highly parallelized, scale-out workloads that require the highest possible throughput to single-threaded, latency-sensitive workloads. Use cases such as lift-and-shift business-critical applications, big data analytics, web serving and content management, application development and testing, media and entertainment workflows, database backups, and container storage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-europe-paris-region/","postDateTime":"2019-06-12T09:53:56Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System is Available in the AWS Europe (Paris) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Europe (Paris) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-asia-pacific-mumbai-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-asia-pacific-mumbai-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:27:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Mumbai) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need – when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies. Amazon EFS is a fully managed service that requires no changes to your existing applications and tools, providing access through a standard file system interface for seamless integration. There is a Standard and an Infrequent Access storage class available with Amazon EFS. Using Lifecycle Management, files not accessed for 30 days will automatically be moved to a cost-optimized Infrequent Access storage class, giving you a simple way to store and access active and infrequently accessed file system data in the same file system while reducing storage costs by up to 85%. Amazon EFS is a regional service storing data within and across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) for high availability and durability. You can access your file systems across AZs, regions, and VPCs and share files between thousands of Amazon EC2 instances and on-premises servers via AWS Direct Connect or AWS VPN.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases from highly parallelized, scale-out workloads that require the highest possible throughput to single-threaded, latency-sensitive workloads. Use cases such as lift-and-shift business-critical applications, big data analytics, web serving and content management, application development and testing, media and entertainment workflows, database backups, and container storage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-asia-pacific-mumbai-region/","postDateTime":"2019-06-05T16:24:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System is Available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Mumbai) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Mumbai) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#storage","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"storage","description":"marketing:marchitecture/storage","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-aws-datasync-now-supports-efs-to-efs-transfer","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/aws-datasync-now-supports-efs-to-efs-transfer/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e to automatically, efficiently, and securely copy files between two \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) resources, including file systems in different AWS Regions and ones owned by different AWS accounts.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;Using DataSync to copy data between EFS file systems, you can perform one-time migrations, periodic ingest for distributed workloads, or automate replication for data protection and recovery, at speeds up to 10 times faster than open-source tools.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS DataSync is an online data transfer service that simplifies, automates, and accelerates copying data between NFS file shares, S3 buckets, and EFS file systems.\u0026nbsp; DataSync uses a software agent to connect to your EFS file systems and automates scaling and validating transfers, so you don’t have write scripts, modify your applications, or manage infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need – when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies. Amazon EFS is a fully managed service that requires no changes to your existing applications and tools, providing access through a standard file system interface for seamless integration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/gs-step-four-sync-files.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eget started\u003c/a\u003e copying data between Amazon EFS file systems using AWS DataSync, first deploy the DataSync agent as an Amazon EC2 instance inside a VPC with access to your source file system.\u0026nbsp; Once you activate the AWS DataSync agent using a web browser, you select Amazon EFS as your destination AWS storage, enter your file system details, and start moving data. To simplify deployment and configuration of the AWS DataSync agent, you can also use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws-samples/amazon-efs-tutorial/tree/master/in-cloud-transfer\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync In-cloud Transfer Quick Start and Scheduler\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing DataSync to copy data between EFS file systems, you \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/datasync/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003epay for the amount of data copied\u003c/a\u003e in addition to the EC2 instance cost for running the DataSync agent. For AWS DataSync and Amazon EFS regional availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. Learn more about AWS DataSync \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e, and try it out in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/aws-datasync-now-supports-efs-to-efs-transfer/","postDateTime":"2019-05-29T10:47:24Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS DataSync Now Supports EFS-to-EFS Transfer","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/datasync.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e to automatically, efficiently, and securely copy files between two \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System\u003c/a\u003e (Amazon EFS) resources, including file systems in different AWS Regions and ones owned by different AWS accounts.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;Using DataSync to copy data between EFS file systems, you can perform one-time migrations, periodic ingest for distributed workloads, or automate replication for data protection and recovery, at speeds up to 10 times faster than open-source tools.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"migration","description":"marketing:marchitecture/migration","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:09:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-datasync","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-datasync","description":"general:products/aws-datasync","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:10+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-elastic-file-system-is-available-in-the-aws-canada-central-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon-elastic-file-system-is-available-in-the-aws-canada-central-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Canada (Central) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need – when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies. Amazon EFS is a fully managed service that requires no changes to your existing applications and tools, providing access through a standard file system interface for seamless integration. There is a Standard and an Infrequent Access storage class available with Amazon EFS. Using Lifecycle Management, files not accessed for 30 days will automatically be moved to a cost-optimized Infrequent Access storage class, giving you a simple way to store and access active and infrequently accessed file system data in the same file system while reducing storage costs by up to 85%. Amazon EFS is a regional service storing data within and across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) for high availability and durability. You can access your file systems across AZs, regions, and VPCs and share files between thousands of Amazon EC2 instances and on-premises servers via AWS Direct Connect or AWS VPN.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases from highly parallelized, scale-out workloads that require the highest possible throughput to single-threaded, latency-sensitive workloads. Use cases such as lift-and-shift business-critical applications, big data analytics, web serving and content management, application development and testing, media and entertainment workflows, database backups, and container storage.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon-elastic-file-system-is-available-in-the-aws-canada-central-region/","postDateTime":"2019-05-01T15:53:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System is Available in the AWS Canada (Central) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Canada (Central) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-04-introducing-aws-backup","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/introducing-aws-backup/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:27:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Sydney) and EU (Frankfurt) Regions. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is a fully managed backup service that makes it easy to centralize and automate the back up of data across AWS services in the cloud as well as on premises. With AWS Backup, protecting your AWS resources, such as Amazon EFS file systems, is as easy as a few clicks in the AWS Backup console. Customers can configure and audit the AWS resources they want to back up, automate backup scheduling, set retention policies, and monitor all recent backup and restore activity.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing AWS Backup, you can centrally configure backup policies and monitor backup activity for AWS resources, such as Amazon EBS volumes, Amazon RDS databases, Amazon DynamoDB tables, Amazon EFS file systems, and AWS Storage Gateway volumes. AWS Backup provides a fully managed, policy-based backup solution, simplifying your backup management, enabling you to meet your business and regulatory backup compliance requirements. As customers build their applications in the AWS Cloud, data can become distributed across multiple AWS services, including database services, block storage, object storage, and file systems. While these services have backup capabilities, customers often create custom scripts to automate backup scheduling, enforce retention policies, and consolidate backup activity across AWS services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is available in the US East (Northern Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Frankfurt), EU (Ireland), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) Regions.\u0026nbsp;For more information on where AWS Backup is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Learn more on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup\u003c/a\u003e page and the latest \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/aws-backup-automate-and-centrally-manage-your-backups/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:07Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/introducing-aws-backup/","postDateTime":"2019-04-04T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Backup is Now Available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Sydney) and EU (Frankfurt) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is now available in the AWS Asia Pacific (Sydney) and EU (Frankfurt) Regions. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-block-store","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-block-store","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-block-store","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-backup","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-backup","description":"general:products/aws-backup","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-dynamodb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-dynamodb","description":"general:products/amazon-dynamodb","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-storage-gateway","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-storage-gateway","description":"general:products/aws-storage-gateway","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:51+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-efs-now-supports-tag-on-create","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-efs-now-supports-tag-on-create/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now tag your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e file system resources as they are created. Previously, you could add tags to your file system resources once they were created.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                Amazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. By assigning tags inline with file system creation, you can more easily enforce authorization, access control, and cost allocation for your EFS resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                You can manage resource tags for your Amazon EFS file systems using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e, CLI, or SDK. AWS resource tags are supported by Amazon EFS in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where EFS is available\u003c/a\u003e at no additional cost. For more information, please visit:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e· \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-fs-tags.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTagging\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon EFS Developer Guide\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e· \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/account-management/aws-tagging-strategies/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Tagging Strategies\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e· \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsaccountbilling/latest/aboutv2/cost-alloc-tags.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUsing Cost Allocation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-efs-now-supports-tag-on-create/","postDateTime":"2019-02-19T12:09:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Now Supports Tag-on-Create","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now tag your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS)\u003c/a\u003e file system resources as they are created. Previously, you could add tags to your file system resources once they were created.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-efs-introduces-lower-cost-storage-class","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-efs-introduces-lower-cost-storage-class/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) is a new storage class for Amazon EFS that is cost-optimized for files that are accessed less frequently.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. Customers can now use EFS IA to more cost-effectively store larger amounts of data in their file systems, expanding their ability to use Amazon EFS to an even wider set of applications. EFS IA reduces storage costs for files not accessed every day, with savings up to 85% compared to the EFS Standard storage class. With EFS IA, customers can now easily and cost-effectively store and access all their files in a file system, eliminating the need to move or delete data to manage costs.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can use EFS IA by creating a new file system and enabling Lifecycle Management. With Lifecycle Management enabled, EFS automatically will move files that have not been accessed for 30 days from the Standard storage class to the Infrequent Access storage class. The EFS IA storage class enables storing infrequently accessed files and actively used files in the same file system without requiring changes to applications or workflows. EFS IA and Lifecycle Management give customers a simple way to store and access file-based data in AWS while significantly reducing storage costs for files not accessed every day.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS IA is ideal for use cases where data isn\u0027t accessed frequently but needs to be readily available. Examples include satisfying audit or retention requirements, performing historical analysis, backup and recovery, and document management/reporting systems. To quickly load data into an EFS file system, we recommend using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/datasync/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS DataSync\u003c/a\u003e, an online data transfer service that makes it easy for you to automate moving data between on-premises storage and EFS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS Infrequent Access\u0026nbsp;is available in all Amazon EFS regions. For pricing information in your region, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS pricing page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information. To learn more, visit the latest \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-infrequent-access-storage-class-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e,\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/faq/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS FAQ page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-efs-introduces-lower-cost-storage-class/","postDateTime":"2019-02-13T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Introduces Lower Cost Storage Class","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS Infrequent Access (EFS IA) is a new storage class for Amazon EFS that is cost-optimized for files that are accessed less frequently.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-europe-london-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-europe-london-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:09:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:36:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Europe (London) Region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need – when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies. Amazon EFS is a fully managed service that requires no changes to your existing applications and tools, providing access through a standard file system interface for seamless integration. Amazon EFS is a regional service storing data within and across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) for high availability and durability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases from highly parallelized, scale-out workloads that require the highest possible throughput to single-threaded, latency-sensitive workloads. Use cases such as lift-and-shift enterprise applications, big data analytics, web serving and content management, application development and testing, media and entertainment workflows, database backups, and container storage.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-efs-is-available-in-the-aws-europe-london-region/","postDateTime":"2019-01-23T11:23:49Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is Available in the AWS Europe (London) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS Europe (London) Region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-introducing-amazon-elastic-file-system-integration-with-aws-backup","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/introducing-amazon-elastic-file-system-integration-with-aws-backup/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                Backup Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) with AWS Backup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                AWS Backup is a fully managed backup service that makes it easy to centralize and automate the back up of data across AWS services in the cloud as well as on premises. With AWS Backup, protecting your AWS resources, such as Amazon EFS file systems, is as easy as a few clicks in the AWS Backup console. Customers can configure and audit the AWS resources they want to back up, automate backup scheduling, set retention policies, and monitor all recent backup and restore activity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS integration with AWS Backup removes the need for costly, customer solutions or manual processes by providing a fully managed, policy based backup solution that provides automated backup scheduling and backup retention management.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS Backup is available in the US East (Northern Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) regions. For more information on where Amazon EFS and AWS Backup is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. For pricing information in your region, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup pricing page\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about Amazon EFS integration with AWS Backup, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/backup/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup product page\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Backup documentation\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/introducing-amazon-elastic-file-system-integration-with-aws-backup/","postDateTime":"2019-01-16T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Elastic File System Integration with AWS Backup","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                Backup Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) with AWS Backup.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-backup","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-backup","description":"general:products/aws-backup","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:45+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-emr-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-emr-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:39:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/emr\"\u003eAmazon EMR\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon EMR.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon EMR available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon EMR does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/emr/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EMR Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon EMR is available. For more information on where Amazon EMR is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/emr/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon EMR. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2021-12-21T18:28:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-emr-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-07T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EMR Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/emr\"\u003eAmazon EMR\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon EMR.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-efs-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-efs-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:14:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for Amazon EFS, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon EFS file systems.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon EFS file systems available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon EFS does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon EFS is available. For more information on where Amazon EFS is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon EFS. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-efs-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-02T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for Amazon EFS, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon EFS file systems.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-12-new-aws-parallelcluster-features","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/new-aws-parallelcluster-features/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:01:31+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThree new features for AWS ParallelCluster, available today, will help customers further simplify the process of creating and managing HPC clusters on Amazon Web Services (AWS).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eAWS Batch Support:\u003c/b\u003e Customers can now use AWS Batch as a job scheduler in AWS ParallelCluster and submit distributed computing jobs through AWS ParallelCluster to AWS Batch. AWS Batch enables developers, scientists, and engineers to easily and efficiently run hundreds of thousands of batch computing jobs on AWS. AWS Batch also supports scheduling multi-node parallel jobs, enabling customers to efficiently run single jobs that span multiple Amazon EC2 instances.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) integration:\u003c/b\u003e AWS ParallelCluster now supports native configuration for EFS to further enhance storage and file management features. Users can create and/or mount EFS directly from AWS ParallelCluster without a post-install script.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eRAID Array Configuration Support:\u003c/b\u003e AWS ParallelCluster customers can now easily create a RAID 0 or RAID 1 array for use with their HPC cluster. RAID 0 combines multiple drives into a single drive to provide enhanced I/O performance, while RAID 1 combines multiple drives into a single drive for better fault tolerance. RAID arrays can be created from up to 5 Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) volumes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS ParallelCluster is available at no additional charge, and you pay only for the AWS resources needed to run your applications. AWS ParallelCluster is released via the Python Package Index (PyPI). AWS ParallelCluster’s source code is hosted under the Amazon Web Services repository on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/aws-parallelcluster\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp; Learn how to launch an HPC cluster using AWS ParallelCluster \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/opensource/aws-parallelcluster/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:23Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/new-aws-parallelcluster-features/","postDateTime":"2018-12-17T16:20:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New AWS ParallelCluster Features","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThree new features for AWS ParallelCluster, available today, will help customers further simplify the process of creating and managing HPC clusters on Amazon Web Services (AWS).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eAWS Batch Support:\u003c/b\u003e Customers can now use AWS Batch as a job scheduler in AWS ParallelCluster and submit distributed computing jobs through AWS ParallelCluster to AWS Batch. AWS Batch enables developers, scientists, and engineers to easily and efficiently run hundreds of thousands of batch computing jobs on AWS. AWS Batch also supports scheduling multi-node parallel jobs, enabling customers to efficiently run single jobs that span multiple Amazon EC2 instances.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (EFS) integration:\u003c/b\u003e AWS ParallelCluster now supports native configuration for EFS to further enhance storage and file management features. Users can create and/or mount EFS directly from AWS ParallelCluster without a post-install script.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eRAID Array Configuration Support:\u003c/b\u003e AWS ParallelCluster customers can now easily create a RAID 0 or RAID 1 array for use with their HPC cluster. RAID 0 combines multiple drives into a single drive to provide enhanced I/O performance, while RAID 1 combines multiple drives into a single drive for better fault tolerance. RAID arrays can be created from up to 5 Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) volumes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS ParallelCluster is available at no additional charge, and you pay only for the AWS resources needed to run your applications. AWS ParallelCluster is released via the Python Package Index (PyPI). AWS ParallelCluster’s source code is hosted under the Amazon Web Services repository on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/aws/aws-parallelcluster\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp; Learn how to launch an HPC cluster using AWS ParallelCluster \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/opensource/aws-parallelcluster/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-use-case#high-performance-computing","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-use-case","name":"high-performance-computing","description":"general:use-case/high-performance-computing","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:28+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-ec2","description":"general:products/amazon-ec2","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-12-amazon-efs-available-in-aws-govcloud-us-west-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/amazon-efs-available-in-aws-govcloud--us-west-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to scale on demand to petabytes without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need – when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent low latencies. Amazon EFS is a fully managed service that requires no changes to your existing applications and tools, providing access through a standard file system interface for seamless integration. Amazon EFS is a regional service storing data within and across multiple Availability Zones (AZs) for high availability and durability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases from highly parallelized, scale-out workloads that require the highest possible throughput to single-threaded, latency-sensitive workloads. Use cases such as lift-and-shift enterprise applications, big data analytics, web serving and content management, application development and testing, media and entertainment workflows, database backups, and container storage.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                  For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/12/amazon-efs-available-in-aws-govcloud--us-west-region/","postDateTime":"2018-12-12T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is Available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-amazon-efs-now-supports-1000-file-systems-per-account","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-efs-now-supports-1000-file-systems-per-account/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:23+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now create up to 1,000 file systems in your AWS account.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources.   You can now create up to 1,000 file systems per AWS account, an increase from the existing limit of 125.  You can also now create up to 400 EFS mount targets per Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional file systems can be created for no additional cost, and you will be billed based on amount of data stored across all file systems. For pricing information in your region, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS pricing page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information. To learn more about Amazon EFS file system limits, please consult the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-efs-now-supports-1000-file-systems-per-account/","postDateTime":"2018-11-28T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now Supports 1000 File Systems per Account","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now create up to 1,000 file systems in your AWS account.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-amazon-efs-now-supports-access-across-accounts-and-vpcs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-efs-now-supports-access-across-accounts-and-vpcs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now connect to an Amazon EFS file system from EC2 instances in a different AWS account or Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides a simple, scalable, elastic file system for Linux-based workloads for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. When you use a VPC peering connection or VPC Transit Gateway to connect VPCs, EC2 instances in one VPC can access EFS file systems in another VPC, even if the VPCs belong to different accounts.  You can also now place EC2 instances owned by one account in the same VPC as an EFS file system owned by a different account using shared VPCs.  This allows applications in different accounts to share a central file system, eliminating the cost and complexity of copying data between VPCs.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccess to Amazon EFS across accounts and VPCs is available in regions where Amazon EFS, VPC peering, VPC Transit Gateway, and shared VPCs are available. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.  You will be billed only for network connectivity, such as any VPC Transit Gateways or VPC peering connections that you create, as well as associated data transfer fees. Intra-region VPC peering is only possible when using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-fs-access-vpc-peering.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecertain instance types\u003c/a\u003e.  To learn more about how to access your Amazon EFS file systems, please consult the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-efs-now-supports-access-across-accounts-and-vpcs/","postDateTime":"2018-11-28T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now Supports Access Across Accounts and VPCs","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now connect to an Amazon EFS file system from EC2 instances in a different AWS account or Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC).\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-amazon-elastic-file-system-now-supports-512-locks-per-file","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-elastic-file-system-now-supports-512-locks-per-file/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports 512 locks per file.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new limit is an increase from 87 locks per file and is available in all regions for new and existing file systems.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe 512-lock limit allows applications to use additional locks enabling higher levels of concurrency and increased performance.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS product page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-elastic-file-system-now-supports-512-locks-per-file/","postDateTime":"2018-11-01T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System Now Supports 512 Locks per File","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports 512 locks per file.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-amazon-efs-now-supports-aws-vpn-and-inter-region-vpc-peering","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/amazon-efs-now-supports-aws-vpn-and-inter-region-vpc-peering/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now connect to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e file systems from EC2 instances in other AWS regions using an inter-region VPC peering connection, and from on-premises servers using an AWS VPN connection.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for AWS VPN complements existing support for AWS Direct Connect, further enabling you to move data between on-premises servers and Amazon EFS.  This allows you to back up your on-premises data to EFS, migrate data sets to EFS, and temporarily burst workloads into AWS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith support for inter-region VPC peering, you can connect EC2 instances in one region to EFS file systems in another.  This allows you to copy frequently-accessed data across regions to optimize performance, and synchronize data across AWS Regions for disaster recovery.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccess to Amazon EFS with AWS VPN and inter-region peering is available in all Amazon EFS regions. There is no additional cost for on-premises or inter-region access to your Amazon EFS file systems. You will be billed for any AWS Direct Connect, AWS VPN, or VPC peering connections that you create, as well as associated data transfer fees. For pricing information in your region, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS pricing page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information. To learn more about how to access your Amazon EFS file systems, please consult the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/amazon-efs-now-supports-aws-vpn-and-inter-region-vpc-peering/","postDateTime":"2018-10-23T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now Supports AWS VPN and Inter-Region VPC Peering","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now connect to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e file systems from EC2 instances in other AWS regions using an inter-region VPC peering connection, and from on-premises servers using an AWS VPN connection.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-08-deploy-corda-enterprise-on-aws-with-new-quick-start","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/deploy-corda-enterprise-on-aws-with-new-quick-start/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:27:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start deploys a Corda Enterprise node on the Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud. The Quick Start was created by APN Partner R3 in collaboration with AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing smart contract and blockchain technology, the Corda platform allows existing  business networks to reduce transaction and record-keeping costs while streamlining business operations. Corda Enterprise on AWS is a production-ready implementation of a Corda Enterprise node, which offers built-in resilience and high availability and which can scale as the needs of the node operator change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start is ideal for IT infrastructure architects, administrators, DevOps professionals, CorDapp developers, or business users who are planning to deploy a Corda Enterprise node on the AWS Cloud.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this Quick Start, Corda Enterprise deployment takes about 30 minutes. The deployment is automated by AWS CloudFormation templates and automatically provisions to the Corda Testnet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quickstart/architecture/r3-corda/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003earchitecture and details\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://fwd.aws/PDyen\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeployment guide\u003c/a\u003e for step-by-step instructions\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDownload the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://fwd.aws/kVDxQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation templates\u003c/a\u003e that automate the deployment from GitHub\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo browse and launch other AWS Quick Start reference deployments, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quickstart/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecomplete catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eQuick Starts are automated reference deployments that use AWS CloudFormation templates to deploy key technologies on AWS, following AWS best practices.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eThis Quick Start was built by R3 in collaboration with AWS solutions architects. R3 is an AWS Partner Network (APN) Partner.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:33Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/deploy-corda-enterprise-on-aws-with-new-quick-start/","postDateTime":"2018-08-16T14:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Deploy Corda Enterprise on AWS with New Quick Start","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start deploys a Corda Enterprise node on the Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud. The Quick Start was created by APN Partner R3 in collaboration with AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#partner-network","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"partner-network","description":"marketing:marchitecture/partner-network","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#aws-quick-start","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"aws-quick-start","description":"marketing:marchitecture/aws-quick-start","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-block-store","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-block-store","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-block-store","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-08-deploy-corda-on-aws-with-new-quick-start","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/deploy-corda-on-aws-with-new-quick-start/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:28:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start deploys a Corda node on the Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud. The Quick Start was created by APN Partner R3 in collaboration with AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing smart contract and blockchain technology, the Corda platform allows existing business networks to reduce transaction and record-keeping costs while streamlining business operations. Corda on AWS is a production-ready implementation of a Corda node, which offers built-in resilience and high availability and which can scale as the needs of the node operator change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start is ideal for IT infrastructure architects, administrators, DevOps professionals, CorDapp developers, or business users who are planning to deploy a Corda node on the AWS Cloud.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this Quick Start, Corda deployment takes about 30 minutes. The deployment is automated by AWS CloudFormation templates and automatically provisions to the Corda Testnet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quickstart/architecture/r3-corda/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003earchitecture and details\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://fwd.aws/PDyen\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeployment guide\u003c/a\u003e for step-by-step instructions\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDownload the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://fwd.aws/kVDxQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation templates\u003c/a\u003e that automate the deployment from GitHub\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo browse and launch other AWS Quick Start reference deployments, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quickstart/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecomplete catalog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eQuick Starts are automated reference deployments that use AWS CloudFormation templates to deploy key technologies on AWS, following AWS best practices.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eThis Quick Start was built by R3 in collaboration with AWS solutions architects. R3 is an AWS Partner Network (APN) Partner.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-24T16:06:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/deploy-corda-on-aws-with-new-quick-start/","postDateTime":"2018-08-16T14:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Deploy Corda on AWS with New Quick Start","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start deploys a Corda node on the Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud. The Quick Start was created by APN Partner R3 in collaboration with AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#aws-quick-start","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"aws-quick-start","description":"marketing:marchitecture/aws-quick-start","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#partner-network","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"partner-network","description":"marketing:marchitecture/partner-network","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elastic-block-store","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elastic-block-store","description":"general:products/amazon-elastic-block-store","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T20:59:48+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-rds","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-rds","description":"general:products/amazon-rds","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:38:13+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-08-amazon-efs-now-available-in-asia-pacific-singapore-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/amazon-efs-now-available-in-asia-pacific-singapore-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:53:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Asia Pacific (Singapore) region.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to elastically scale on demand without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS that scale as a file system grows, with consistent low latencies. As a regional service, Amazon EFS is designed for high availability and durability storing data redundantly across multiple Availability Zones.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these capabilities, Amazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases, including web serving and content management, enterprise applications, media and entertainment processing workflows, home directories, database backups, developer tools, container storage, and big data analytics workloads.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can move data securely and quickly from existing on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS with the EFS File Sync feature simplifying migrations and speeding time to production.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/amazon-efs-now-available-in-asia-pacific-singapore-region/","postDateTime":"2018-08-15T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Now Available in Asia Pacific (Singapore) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Asia Pacific (Singapore) region.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-amazon-efs-achieves-pci-dss-compliance","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-efs-achieves-pci-dss-compliance/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:23:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now a Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) compliant service.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now store sensitive payment card data in an encrypted Amazon EFS file system for use cases such as payment processing, mobile wallet, and payment fraud prevention that are subject to PCI DSS compliance.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePCI DSS is a proprietary information security standard administered by the PCI Security Standards Council and applies to all entities that store, process or transmit cardholder data and/or sensitive authentication data including merchants, processors, acquirers, issuers, and service providers.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources. It is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. Amazon EFS is built to elastically scale on demand without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it. It is designed to provide massively parallel shared access to thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS that scale as a file system grows, with consistent low latencies. As a regional service, Amazon EFS is designed for high availability and durability storing data redundantly across multiple Availability Zones.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith these capabilities, Amazon EFS is well suited to support a broad spectrum of use cases, including web serving and content management, enterprise applications, media and entertainment processing workflows, home directories, database backups, developer tools, container storage, and big data analytics workloads. Customers can move data securely and quickly from existing on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS with the EFS File Sync feature simplifying migrations and speeding time to production.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/pci-dss-level-1-faqs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLearn\u003c/a\u003e more about PCI DSS Certification, and visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-efs-achieves-pci-dss-compliance/","postDateTime":"2018-07-13T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Achieves PCI DSS Compliance","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now a Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) compliant service.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-amazon-efs-now-supports-provisioned-throughput","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-efs-now-supports-provisioned-throughput/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:55:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing Provisioned Throughput for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS now allows you to instantly provision the throughput required for your applications independent of the amount of data stored in your file system, allowing you to optimize throughput for your application’s performance needs. You can use Amazon EFS for applications with a wide range of performance requirements. Until today, the amount of throughput an application could demand from Amazon EFS was based on the amount of data stored in the file system. This default Amazon EFS throughput bursting mode offers a simple experience that is suitable for a majority of applications. Now with Provisioned Throughput, applications with throughput requirements greater than those allowed by Amazon EFS’s default throughput bursting mode can achieve the throughput levels required immediately and consistently independent of the amount of data. You can quickly configure throughput of your file system with a few simple steps using the AWS Console, AWS CLI or AWS API.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Provisioned Throughput, you will be billed separately for the amount of storage used and for the throughput provisioned beyond what you are entitled to through the default Amazon EFS Bursting Throughput mode.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProvisioned Throughput is available in all Amazon EFS regions. For pricing information in your region, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS pricing page\u003c/a\u003e, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/globalinfrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information. To learn more, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/throughput-modes.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct documentation\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/faq/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS FAQ page\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:09Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-efs-now-supports-provisioned-throughput/","postDateTime":"2018-07-12T13:35:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Now Supports Provisioned Throughput","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are announcing Provisioned Throughput for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-asia-pacific-tokyo-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-asia-pacific-tokyo-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:47:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Asia Pacific (Tokyo) region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) provides simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources via AWS Direct Connect. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to quickly create and configure file systems. It provides massively parallel shared access for thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent, low latencies. Amazon EFS is built to elastically scale on demand without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a regional service designed for high availability and durability supporting a broad spectrum of use cases, including web serving and content management, enterprise applications, media and entertainment processing workflows, home directories, database backups, developer tools, container storage, and big data and analytics applications. Customers can move data securely and quickly from existing on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS with the EFS File Sync feature simplifying migrations and speeding time to production.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-asia-pacific-tokyo-region/","postDateTime":"2018-07-11T09:45:33Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Available in Asia Pacific (Tokyo) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Asia Pacific (Tokyo) region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-amazon-efs-now-a-hipaa-eligible-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/amazon-efs-now-a-hipaa-eligible-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are adding Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) to our list of HIPAA Eligible Services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this addition, customers that have a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) with AWS can now store healthcare-related file data, including encrypted Protected Health Information (PHI), in an Amazon EFS file system. By providing a secure and encrypted file system, Amazon EFS can now be used as a part of applications that need to store research, genetics, informatics, or imaging data containing PHI.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with the AWS Cloud and on-premises resources via AWS Direct Connect. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to quickly create and configure file systems. It provides massively parallel shared access for thousands of Amazon EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent, low latencies. Amazon EFS is built to elastically scale on demand without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a regional service designed for high availability and durability supporting a broad spectrum of use cases, including web serving and content management, enterprise applications, media and entertainment processing workflows, home directories, database backups, developer tools, container storage, and big data and analytics applications. Customers can move data securely and quickly from existing on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS with the EFS File Sync feature simplifying migrations and speeding time to production.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you already have a BAA with AWS, you can use Amazon EFS immediately to transfer data into your HIPAA accounts. You must ensure that all PHI stored in Amazon EFS is encrypted in transit and at rest.\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/health/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLearn\u003c/a\u003e more about building healthcare applications on AWS, and visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/amazon-efs-now-a-hipaa-eligible-service/","postDateTime":"2018-05-31T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now a HIPAA-Eligible Service","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we are adding Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) to our list of HIPAA Eligible Services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-04-amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-in-transit","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-in-transit/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:46:19+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now allows you to encrypt data in transit between your file system and its clients. The Amazon EFS encryption of data in transit feature uses industry-standard Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2 to encrypt all data sent to and from connected clients. To further simplify using EFS, a new mount helper utility is available that can be used to establish encrypted client connections to either encrypted at rest or unencrypted file systems. With this launch, Amazon EFS now offers a comprehensive encryption solution, allowing customers to encrypt their data both at rest and in transit.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, simply sign into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e and follow the instructions to download the EFS mount helper. To learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/encryption.html#encryption-in-transit\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS encryption in transit section\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon EFS User Guide and to see examples of how encryption can be used to enhance your security \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-encryption-of-data-in-transit-for-amazon-efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eclick here\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEncryption of data in transit is available at no additional cost in all Amazon EFS regions. For more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/04/amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-in-transit/","postDateTime":"2018-04-04T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Now Supports Encryption of Data in Transit","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now allows you to encrypt data in transit between your file system and its clients. The Amazon EFS encryption of data in transit feature uses industry-standard Transport Layer Security (TLS) 1.2 to encrypt all data sent to and from connected clients. To further simplify using EFS, a new mount helper utility is available that can be used to establish encrypted client connections to either encrypted at rest or unencrypted file systems. With this launch, Amazon EFS now offers a comprehensive encryption solution, allowing customers to encrypt their data both at rest and in transit.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-03-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-us-west-northern-california-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-us-west-northern-california-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the US West (Northern California) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) provides simple, scalable, elastic file storage for use with AWS Cloud services and on-premises resources via AWS Direct Connect. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. It provides massively parallel access for thousands of EC2 instances, enabling your applications to achieve high levels of aggregate throughput and IOPS with consistent, low latencies. Amazon EFS is built to elastically scale on demand without disrupting applications, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is a regional service designed for high availability and durability supporting a broad spectrum of uses cases, including web serving and content management, enterprise applications, media and entertainment processing workflows, home directories, database backups, developer tools, container storage, and big data and analytics applications.\u0026nbsp;Customers can move data securely and quickly from existing on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS with the EFS File Sync feature simplifying migrations and speeding time to production.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e product page, and see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for complete regional availability information.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:28Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-us-west-northern-california-region/","postDateTime":"2018-03-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Available in US West (Northern California) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the US West (Northern California) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-12-efs-file-sync-now-available-in-all-amazon-efs-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/efs-file-sync-now-available-in-all-amazon-efs-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:15:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eEFS File Sync for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in two additional AWS Regions: Asia Pacific (Sydney), and EU (Frankfurt).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud. EFS File Sync provides an affordable way to efficiently and securely move data from on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS, with simple setup and management in the AWS Console, at speeds of up to 5x faster than standard Linux copy tools.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is available today in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where EFS is offered. To get started using EFS File Sync, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/faq/#filesync\"\u003ethe FAQ\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/12/efs-file-sync-now-available-in-all-amazon-efs-regions/","postDateTime":"2017-12-13T11:43:35Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"EFS File Sync Now Available in All Amazon EFS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eEFS File Sync for Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in two additional AWS Regions: Asia Pacific (Sydney), and EU (Frankfurt).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-11-sync-files-to-amazon-elastic-file-system-quickly-easily-and-securely-with-efs-file-sync","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/sync-files-to-amazon-elastic-file-system-quickly-easily-and-securely-with-efs-file-sync/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:45:15+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use EFS File Sync to efficiently and securely sync files from on-premises or in-cloud file systems to Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) at speeds of up to 5x faster than standard Linux copy tools. Amazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePrior to EFS File Sync, customers that wanted to copy data from existing file storage into Amazon EFS had to choose between standard Linux copy tools that could be slow and require manual configuration, or commercial products that lack direct ingest to Amazon EFS. EFS File Sync provides a fast, simple, and affordable way to securely move data from existing on-premises or in-cloud file systems into Amazon EFS, with simple setup and management in the AWS Console.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePricing for EFS File Sync is simple. You pay per-GB for data copied to Amazon EFS. For more information see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/#filesync\"\u003eAmazon EFS File Sync Pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEFS File Sync is available in the US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) regions, with availability in the EU (Frankfurt) and Asia Pacific (Sydney) regions coming in December 2017.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo use EFS File Sync, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/efs/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS Console\u003c/a\u003e to get started.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nTo learn more, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/faq/#filesync\"\u003evisit the FAQ\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:54:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/sync-files-to-amazon-elastic-file-system-quickly-easily-and-securely-with-efs-file-sync/","postDateTime":"2017-11-22T15:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Sync Files to Amazon Elastic File System Quickly, Easily and Securely with EFS File Sync","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use EFS File Sync to efficiently and securely sync files from on-premises or in-cloud file systems to Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) at speeds of up to 5x faster than standard Linux copy tools. Amazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-08-amazon-efs-now-supports-additional-permissions-for-finer-grained-control-of-directory-and-file-access","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-efs-now-supports-additional-permissions-for-finer-grained-control-of-directory-and-file-access/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:28:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports the use of setgid and sticky bit special permissions on directories. This new capability allows you to further customize access permissions for shared directories across a set of file system users. When the\u0026nbsp;setgid\u0026nbsp;permission is set on a directory, files created in the directory belong to the group associated with the directory (instead of the group to which the user creating the file belongs). The\u0026nbsp;sticky bit\u0026nbsp;is used to restrict deletion and renaming of files to the owner of the file or directory or to the root user.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS also now supports running binary files that are configured as execute-only. This capability allows you to configure access permissions for executable files such that they can be only executed and not read or written.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                  These features are available on all new and existing file systems at no additional cost in all Amazon EFS regions. Please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e to see the full list of supported regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-efs-now-supports-additional-permissions-for-finer-grained-control-of-directory-and-file-access/","postDateTime":"2017-08-25T09:09:12Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS now Supports Additional Permissions for Finer-Grained Control of Directory and File Access","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports the use of setgid and sticky bit special permissions on directories. This new capability allows you to further customize access permissions for shared directories across a set of file system users. When the\u0026nbsp;setgid\u0026nbsp;permission is set on a directory, files created in the directory belong to the group associated with the directory (instead of the group to which the user creating the file belongs). The\u0026nbsp;sticky bit\u0026nbsp;is used to restrict deletion and renaming of files to the owner of the file or directory or to the root user.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-08-amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-at-rest","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-at-rest/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:09:21+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                 Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) now allows you to encrypt your data at rest using keys managed through AWS Key Management Service (KMS). Encryption and decryption are handled seamlessly, so you don’t have to modify your applications to access your data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                 When you create a new file system, you can choose to enable encryption via the AWS Management Console or API. To encrypt your data, you can use the default EFS key automatically created in your account or a key you generated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e               Encryption at rest is available at no additional cost in all Amazon EFS regions. Please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/pricing/\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e to see the full list of supported regions. AWS KMS usage is billed at standard rates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, read the Amazon EFS Encryption \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-encryption-at-rest-for-amazon-elastic-file-system-efs/\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/faq/#encryption\"\u003eAmazon EFS Encryption FAQ\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:13Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/08/amazon-efs-now-supports-encryption-of-data-at-rest/","postDateTime":"2017-08-14T18:18:25Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Now Supports Encryption of Data at Rest","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                 Amazon Elastic File System (EFS) now allows you to encrypt your data at rest using keys managed through AWS Key Management Service (KMS). Encryption and decryption are handled seamlessly, so you don’t have to modify your applications to access your data.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-07-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-eu-frankfurt-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/07/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-eu-frankfurt-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:37:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the EU (Frankfurt) region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/faqs/#efs\"\u003eAmazon EC2 instances\u003c/a\u003e in the AWS Cloud. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. With Amazon EFS, storage capacity is elastic, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS is designed for high availability and durability, and provides performance for a broad spectrum of workloads and applications, including Big Data and analytics, media processing workflows, content management, web serving, and home directories.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can also access your Amazon EFS filesystems directly from on-premises servers over AWS Direct Connect, allowing you to migrate data sets to EFS, enable cloud bursting scenarios, or back up your on-premises data to EFS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e               Amazon EFS is also available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), and Asia Pacific (Sydney). Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e for more information.    \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:53:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/07/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-eu-frankfurt-region/","postDateTime":"2017-07-20T16:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Available in EU (Frankfurt) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the EU (Frankfurt) region.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-03-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-asia-pacific-sydney-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-asia-pacific-sydney-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:39:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Asia Pacific (Sydney) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. With Amazon EFS, storage capacity is elastic, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon EFS is designed for high availability and durability, and provides performance for a broad spectrum of workloads and applications, including Big Data and analytics, media processing workflows, content management, web serving, and home directories.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    You can also access your Amazon EFS filesystems directly from on-premises servers over AWS Direct Connect, allowing you to migrate data sets to EFS, enable cloud bursting scenarios, or back up your on-premises data to EFS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon EFS is also available in US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland). Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:52:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-available-in-asia-pacific-sydney-region/","postDateTime":"2017-03-21T13:12:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Available in Asia Pacific (Sydney) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is now available in the Asia Pacific (Sydney) region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-03-amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-now-supports-nfsv4-lock-upgrading-and-downgrading","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-now-supports-nfsv4-lock-upgrading-and-downgrading/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:21:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports NFS version 4 lock upgrading and downgrading functionality. This new capability extends support in Amazon EFS for the NFSv4.1 and NFSv4.0 protocols by allowing you to run applications that upgrade a read lock atomically to a write lock and downgrade a write lock atomically to a read lock. One example is SQLite, a popular library that’s embedded into many applications and programming language tools like Python and PHP.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    There is no charge to use this feature and it is immediately available in all Amazon EFS regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:52:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/03/amazon-elastic-file-system-amazon-efs-now-supports-nfsv4-lock-upgrading-and-downgrading/","postDateTime":"2017-03-06T07:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) Now Supports NFSv4 Lock Upgrading and Downgrading","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) now supports NFS version 4 lock upgrading and downgrading functionality. This new capability extends support in Amazon EFS for the NFSv4.1 and NFSv4.0 protocols by allowing you to run applications that upgrade a read lock atomically to a write lock and downgrade a write lock atomically to a read lock. One example is SQLite, a popular library that’s embedded into many applications and programming language tools like Python and PHP.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-01-aws-elastic-beanstalk-extensions-for-amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/01/aws-elastic-beanstalk-extensions-for-amazon-efs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:43:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Elastic Beanstalk extends support to Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). You can now create and mount Amazon EFS file systems from within Elastic Beanstalk environments. Using the Elastic Beanstalk extensions for Amazon EFS, you can more easily deploy and scale applications that require shared, scalable, and highly available persistent storage.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eView the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/services-efs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e for more information about how to use the Elastic Beanstalk extensions for EFS.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/01/aws-elastic-beanstalk-extensions-for-amazon-efs/","postDateTime":"2017-01-30T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk Extensions for Amazon EFS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS Elastic Beanstalk extends support to Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS). You can now create and mount Amazon EFS file systems from within Elastic Beanstalk environments. Using the Elastic Beanstalk extensions for Amazon EFS, you can more easily deploy and scale applications that require shared, scalable, and highly available persistent storage.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-elastic-beanstalk","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-elastic-beanstalk","description":"general:products/aws-elastic-beanstalk","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-12-simplified-mounting-of-amazon-efs-file-systems","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/simplified-mounting-of-amazon-efs-file-systems/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:23:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:52+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), which provides simple and scalable file storage in the AWS Cloud, now provides a simpler way for you to mount your file systems on EC2 instances.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen mounting a file system, you can now use a regional DNS name rather than an AZ-specific DNS name. That means that you no longer need to be aware of which AZ your EC2 instances are in when providing a DNS name in your mount command.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis feature is immediately available in the following regions: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about the simplified EFS experience, please consult the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs-mount-cmd-dns-name.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/simplified-mounting-of-amazon-efs-file-systems/","postDateTime":"2016-12-20T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Simplified Mounting of Amazon EFS File Systems","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), which provides simple and scalable file storage in the AWS Cloud, now provides a simpler way for you to mount your file systems on EC2 instances.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-12-amazon-efs-introduces-the-ability-to-access-amazon-efs-file-systems-from-on-premises-servers-via-aws-direct-connect","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-efs-introduces-the-ability-to-access-amazon-efs-file-systems-from-on-premises-servers-via-aws-direct-connect/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:14+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), which provides simple and scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud, now allows you to access your file data from on-premises datacenters. On-premises servers can now move file data to and from your Amazon EFS file systems when connected to your Amazon VPC with AWS Direct Connect, allowing you to migrate data sets to EFS, enable cloud bursting scenarios, or backup your on-premises data to EFS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn-Premises access to EFS is immediately available in the following regions: US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    There is no additional cost for on-premises access to your Amazon EFS file systems. You will be billed for the AWS Direct Connect connection between your on-premises datacenter and your Amazon VPC.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    To learn how to use AWS Direct Connect to allow access for your on-premises servers to Amazon EFS file systems, please consult the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/how-it-works.html#how-it-works-direct-connect\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-efs-introduces-the-ability-to-access-amazon-efs-file-systems-from-on-premises-servers-via-aws-direct-connect/","postDateTime":"2016-12-05T15:12:26Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Introduces the Ability to Access Amazon EFS File Systems from On-premises Servers via AWS Direct Connect","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), which provides simple and scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud, now allows you to access your file data from on-premises datacenters. On-premises servers can now move file data to and from your Amazon EFS file systems when connected to your Amazon VPC with AWS Direct Connect, allowing you to migrate data sets to EFS, enable cloud bursting scenarios, or backup your on-premises data to EFS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-11-amazon-efs-introduces-the-ability-to-access-amazon-efs-file-systems-from-on-premises-servers-via-aws-direct-connect","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/amazon-efs-introduces-the-ability-to-access-amazon-efs-file-systems-from-on-premises-servers-via-aws-direct-connect/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), which provides simple and scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud, now allows you to access your file data from on-premises datacenters. On-premises servers can now move file data to and from your Amazon EFS file systems when connected to your Amazon VPC with AWS Direct Connect, allowing you to migrate data sets to EFS, enable cloud bursting scenarios, or backup your on-premises data to EFS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn-Premises access to EFS is immediately available in the following regions: US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    There is no additional cost for on-premises access to your Amazon EFS file systems. You will be billed for the AWS Direct Connect connection between your on-premises datacenter and your Amazon VPC.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    To learn how to use AWS Direct Connect to allow access for your on-premises servers to Amazon EFS file systems, please consult the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/how-it-works.html#how-it-works-direct-connect\"\u003eAmazon EFS documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/11/amazon-efs-introduces-the-ability-to-access-amazon-efs-file-systems-from-on-premises-servers-via-aws-direct-connect/","postDateTime":"2016-11-30T15:12:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon EFS Introduces the Ability to Access Amazon EFS File Systems from On-premises Servers via AWS Direct Connect","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS), which provides simple and scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud, now allows you to access your file data from on-premises datacenters. On-premises servers can now move file data to and from your Amazon EFS file systems when connected to your Amazon VPC with AWS Direct Connect, allowing you to migrate data sets to EFS, enable cloud bursting scenarios, or backup your on-premises data to EFS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-06-amazon-elastic-file-system-efs-is-now-generally-available","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/06/amazon-elastic-file-system-efs-is-now-generally-available/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. With Amazon EFS, storage capacity is elastic, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  When mounted to Amazon EC2 instances, an Amazon EFS file system provides a standard file system interface and file system access semantics, allowing you to seamlessly integrate Amazon EFS with your existing applications and tools. Multiple Amazon EC2 instances can access an Amazon EFS file system at the same time, allowing Amazon EFS to provide a common data source for workloads and applications running on more than one Amazon EC2 instance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  It’s designed for high availability and durability, and provides performance for a broad spectrum of workloads and applications, including Big Data and analytics, media processing workflows, content management, web serving, and home directories.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon EFS, read the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-elastic-file-system-production-ready-in-three-regions\"\u003eAWS blog\u003c/a\u003e and visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/getting-started.html\"\u003eGetting Started with Amazon EFS\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:49Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/06/amazon-elastic-file-system-efs-is-now-generally-available/","postDateTime":"2016-06-29T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is Now Generally Available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS provides simple, scalable file storage for use with Amazon EC2 instances in the AWS Cloud. Amazon EFS is easy to use and offers a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. With Amazon EFS, storage capacity is elastic, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-04-introducing-amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/04/introducing-amazon-efs/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:19:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:36:36+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is a file storage service for Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances. Amazon EFS is easy to use and provides a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. With Amazon EFS, storage capacity is elastic, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon EFS supports the Network File System version 4 (NFSv4) protocol, so the applications and tools that you use today work seamlessly with Amazon EFS. Multiple Amazon EC2 instances can access an Amazon EFS file system at the same time, providing a common data source for workloads and applications running on more than one instance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With Amazon EFS, you pay only for the storage used by your file system. You don’t need to provision storage in advance and there is no minimum fee or setup cost. Amazon EFS is designed for a wide variety of use cases like content repositories, development environments, and home directories. With on-demand scaling and performance, Amazon EFS is an ideal solution for Big Data applications. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  The Amazon EFS Preview will be available soon. To learn more and request an invite to the Amazon EFS Preview visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/efs/\"\u003ehttp://aws.amazon.com/efs.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/04/introducing-amazon-efs/","postDateTime":"2015-04-09T17:29:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon EFS","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) is a file storage service for Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) instances. Amazon EFS is easy to use and provides a simple interface that allows you to create and configure file systems quickly and easily. With Amazon EFS, storage capacity is elastic, growing and shrinking automatically as you add and remove files, so your applications have the storage they need, when they need it. \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-efs","description":"general:products/amazon-efs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:44+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":124,"totalHits":124},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}